window.SLIME_DOC_INDEX=[{"title": "Balance Reference", "url": "BALANCE.html", "text": "Balance Reference Values describe loaded gameplay ticks, normally 20 per second. Actual survival difficulty and economy depend on play conditions. Growth and incubation Default natural growth needs 12,000 loaded ticks under valid care conditions. Each manual incubator cycle takes 200 ticks , charging one food and one supplement only at completion. Supplement Growth per cycle Cycles for a default newborn Processing time Foods / supplements Breeding Gel 1,200 10 100 seconds 10 / 10 Genetic Catalyst 2,400 5 50 seconds 5 / 5 Royal Gel 3,600 4 40 seconds 4 / 4 These totals exclude gathering, crafting, menu use, and intervals between clicks. Chronological age increases by only 2,000 / 1,000 / 800 ticks respectively. New growthTicks settings affect future births; existing juveniles retain their duration. Bosses Health is measured in points; two points equal one heart. All encounters announce attacks and check distance, height, and cover. Rituals prevent overlapping bosses within 96 blocks. Boss Health Armor Attack families Raw damage by phase Gelatinous King 600 10 4 12 / 16.8 Magmatic Heart 750 12 4 12 / 16.8; eruptions 10 / 14 Crystalline Colossus 900 16 4 10 / 14 Primordial Slime 1,024 14 5 10 / 14 / 19.6 Damage uses base × 2 × 1.4^phase × setting . At multiplier 2, the largest hit reaches 39.2 before defenses. Water halves Magmatic Heart damage after this calculation. Prepared attacks keep their starting phase parameters. The King maintains up to six minions: guards have 36 health and four base damage with Weakness II; healers have 26 health and restore 14 health per 80 ticks; spitters have 28 health and three base damage with Slowness I and Poison I. The Heart supports up to four fire/magma servants; Primordial supports up to three flying echoes. A player-credited victory yields two boss materials: Royal Gel, Igneous Fragment, Prismatic Shard, or Primordial Essence. Minions do not drop loot or XP or split. See boss encounters . Training and symbiosis Action Cost Recovery Lesson 5 energy, +3 hunger, up to +1 trust 200 ticks Water + Moss crop growth 6 energy, +3 hunger per partner Shared 400 ticks Electric + Iron processing 2 energy, +1 hunger per partner Shared 20 ticks Lessons grant 4 + floor(sociability × 4) + floor(stability × 2) points, capped at 100. Wait needs 20, Follow 40, Return home 60. Symbiosis adds up to four machine ticks or one crop stage without bypassing materials or permissions. See companions . Jobs and circuits Fire adds up to 20 furnace ticks per 20-tick helper cooldown for 2 energy and +1 hunger. Fungal converts eight compostables to one bone meal in 200 work ticks for 6 energy and +3 hunger. Abyssal restores up to 60 air and 300 ticks of Night Vision within six blocks for 2 energy and +1 hunger, recovering for 40 ticks. Amber holds three compartments of up to 16 items with no storage cost. Electric pulses need training 20 and cost 2 energy and +1 hunger, with strength 15, intervals 20/40/80/160 ticks, and durations 2/4/8/10. Crystal sonar needs training 20, reaches 12 blocks, and costs 4 energy and +2 hunger only on an echo, with 200-tick recovery even without one. Energized Crystal needs training 40 and one energy initially and per active second, relaying analog 0–15 across 4–32 blocks. Glass displays one item with free 1.5× visual enlargement. Job details · Additional jobs · Signal jobs · Configuration Companion combat All 47 skills have tiered costs and recoveries. Healing: one per ally per 40 ticks, at most six health per activation. Shields: four/eight health for 100 ticks with a shared 200-tick renewal lock. Freeze: 20 ticks after three applications, followed by 120 ticks of protection. Non-royal servants have 32 health. Existing bosses with canonical attributes migrate while preserving their health ratio; customized administrative attributes remain intact."}, {"title": "Configuration", "url": "CONFIGURATION.html", "text": "Configuration Server rules are authoritative NeoForge SERVER options synchronized on login. Stop the server before editing <world>/serverconfig/slimeevolution-server.toml . Use defaultconfigs/ for new-world defaults and back up before changing versions. The Mods configuration screen uses NeoForge's editor; remote-server values are read-only for clients. Twenty ticks normally equal one loaded second. Unloaded chunks do not advance growth or cooldowns. NeoForge corrects out-of-range values. Generated files include comments and limits; review them when upgrading. World-generation changes affect new terrain only. Server settings TOML key Default; minimum; maximum Purpose naturalSpawning true Natural spawning; commands and eggs remain usable when disabled localPopulationLimit 8; 1; 64 Natural-spawn population limit within 32 blocks; does not remove existing slimes spawnChance 0.25; 0; 1 Additional spawn probability after normal checks damageMultiplier 1; 0; 4 Ordinary slime contact and Crystal projectile damage; excludes bosses abilityParticles true Server ability particles; boss ground warnings remain available combat.activeAbilities true Active contact abilities and environmental regeneration; passive defenses remain combat.abilitySounds true Ability activation sounds combat.thermalReactions true Fire removes mod chill; icy contact extinguishes burning targets instead of chilling combat.effectDurationMultiplier 1; 0; 4 Ignition, mud, and chill duration; capped at 200 ticks per application combat.healingMultiplier 1; 0; 4 Healing combined with regeneration genetics; capped at six health combat.mineralImpactReduction 0.25; 0; 0.5 Pre-armor projectile/explosion reduction, genetically adjusted; capped at 75% combat.metalMeleeReduction 0.2; 0; 0.5 Iron melee reduction before genetics; excludes projectiles, explosions, and bypass damage combat.obsidianBlastReduction 0.5; 0; 0.5 Genetically adjusted explosion reduction; capped at 75% combat.iceFireMultiplier 1.5; 1; 4 Fire damage received by Ice slimes combat.wetFireDamage 1; 0; 4 Fire slime damage per loaded second while wet combat.dischargeDamage 2; 0; 4 Wild discharge base, doubled when wet and capped at six. Companion electrical attacks scale relative to default 2, with a 50% wet-target bonus combat.waterConduction true Wet-target discharges may chain to two nearby visible wet targets breeding.enabled true Caretaker-initiated breeding breeding.localPopulationLimit 12; 2; 64 Loaded living slimes within 32 blocks of a birth breeding.recoveryTicks 6000; 200; 240000 Parent recovery, adjusted by fertility breeding.growthTicks 12000; 200; 240000 Growth duration for new juveniles; existing ones retain their duration breeding.mutationChance 0.02; 0; 0.25 Per-allele chance adjusted by stability and unstable parents breeding.mutationStep 0.1; 0; 0.25 Maximum absolute allele mutation; results clamped to 0–1 evolution.metamorphosis true Environmental exposure and catalyst transformations ecology.foraging true Seek loose diet items without gaining trust; respects mobGriefing ecology.grouping true Compatible grouping by species and caretaker, adjusted by sociability ecology.territories true Territorial defense with caretaker and boundary rules ecology.surfaceNests true New-terrain surface nests and finite founders ecology.caveColonies true New-terrain underground colonies and finite founders ecology.nestRarity 24; 1; 1000 Additional one-in-N chance per nest attempt ecology.colonyRarity 12; 1; 1000 Additional one-in-N chance per colony attempt structures.enabled true Generate the six special sites in new chunks structures.crystalCaverns true New Crystal Caverns structures.gelatinousLakes true New Gelatinous Lakes structures.elementalSanctuaries true New Elemental Sanctuaries structures.researcherRuins true New Researcher Ruins structures.ancestralChambers true New Ancestral Chambers structures.royalCourts true New Royal Courts structures.rarity 1; 1; 1000 Additional deterministic one-in-N generation filter bosses.enabled true Start rituals; disabling does not remove existing encounters bosses.damageMultiplier 1; 0; 2 Boss and servant damage; zero disables their damage companions.training true Companion commands available from level 1; existing key retained for compatibility companions.symbiosis true Water + Moss and Electric + Iron cooperation companions.specializations true The 19 individual jobs and new storage deposits Disabling companion features preserves levels, XP, home, preferences, and belongings. Free, disabling cooperation, and item withdrawal remain accessible. Terrain work respects caretaker permissions and mobGriefing . Arena protection persists even when generation is disabled. Rarity filters do not replace datapack spacing and biome rules. Client visuals Local config/slimeevolution-client.toml settings do not change server gameplay. NeoForge's screen provides English and Portuguese labels and help. Key Default / range Effect reducedMotion false Reduces breathing, sway, pulses, and decorative flame, lightning, and steam motion; physical jumps remain visible visualParticleIntensity 0.75 , range 0–1 Extra action and idle elemental particles; zero disables them Extra particles respect Minecraft's particle setting and server abilityParticles . Decorative animation is reduced after 24 blocks and stops after 48, without changing genetics, damage, collision, or world lighting. Geometric flames, electrical arcs, and steam remain visible with minimal particles; their motion follows reducedMotion . The global extra-particle budget is four per five ticks, or two with reduced particles. Actions take priority over idle accents; reduced motion also disables idle accents. Companion rules · Balance"}, {"title": "Installation and Updates", "url": "INSTALLATION.html", "text": "Installation and Updates Requirements Component Required version Minecraft Java Edition 1.21.1 NeoForge 21.1.264 Java 21 GeckoLib 4.9.3 for NeoForge / Minecraft 1.21.1 Install Slime Evolution and GeckoLib on both the client and server , using matching versions for every participant. GeckoLib is a required external dependency; the game cannot load the mod without it. Install Install compatible Minecraft and NeoForge in a separate profile. Close the game or stop the server. Place the Slime Evolution and GeckoLib .jar files in mods/ . Start a test world and check the items, species, and recipes. Read getting started and configuration . The release ZIP includes the official GeckoLib JAR under dependencies/ . Put the JARs in mods/ , not the documentation ZIP. Compare transferred files against the release's SHA256SUMS . GeckoLib keeps its MIT license, supplied under licenses/GECKOLIB_LICENSE in the bundle. Update and back up Stop the server and make a complete, consistent backup of the world, including player data, saved data, dimensions, and server configuration. Keep the previous mod JAR and your mod list. Replace the JAR and test a copy of your world before continuing. Do not downgrade a world after opening it with a newer version. Capsules depend on data/slimeevolution_captures.dat , inventories, and world entities. The Slimepedia uses data/slimeevolution_research.dat in the Overworld. Restoring only an inventory or only a ledger can invalidate capsules or reintroduce old tokens. Minecraft world files do not form a single atomic transaction."}, {"title": "Slime Evolution — Images and Description", "url": "PRESENTATION.html", "text": "Slime Evolution — Images and Description Cover Landscape — 1920×1080 · Square — 1080×1080 Real Minecraft capture with the mod's models: Prismatic at the bottom, Coral in the middle, and Solar on top. Capture post-processing adds soft glow, depth haze, and warm color. The square version is cropped from the original. Banner Original — 2560×960 · Web — 1920×720 The banner features Coral, Prismatic, Solar, Abyssal, Ice, Ferrofluid, Hive, and Aurora, plus the Slimepedia, analyzer, capsule, Prismatic Shard, Ancestral Essence, crown, Genetic Station, Incubator, and Feeder. All are real in-game elements. Short description Discover 47 slime species, breed unique genetic lineages, unlock evolutions, train helpful companions, and challenge four bosses in a SolarPunk-inspired world. Full description A world of slimes to discover, care for, and evolve. Slime Evolution brings 47 species with distinct appearances, habitats, behaviors, and abilities. Find elemental creatures and discover rare lineages through breeding and metamorphosis. Every slime has its own genetics. Combine individuals, follow inherited traits, and explore new possibilities each generation. Learn diets, meet their needs, and develop a bond through care and training. Your slimes can also help with everyday tasks. Nineteen individual jobs cover item transport, irrigation, lighting, repairs, redstone circuits, mineral detection, and more. Certain species cooperate through symbiosis. Explore natural structures, prepare rituals, and challenge four bosses in dedicated arenas. Use the Slimepedia and research equipment to record discoveries and reach advanced lineages. Custom GeckoLib models and animations meet SolarPunk-inspired equipment and interfaces, combining nature, research, and technology. Choose your companions and discover how far the next generation can go. Compatibility Minecraft Java 1.21.1 , NeoForge 21.1.264 , and Java 21 . Requires GeckoLib 4.9.3 on both client and server. The cover's capture shader is not needed to play."}, {"title": "Slime Evolution Guide", "url": "index.html", "text": "Discover, care for, breed, and evolve 47 slime species . Build genetic lineages, train companions, organize helpful workers, and face four bosses in a SolarPunk-inspired world. For Minecraft Java 1.21.1 , NeoForge 21.1.264 , and Java 21 . GeckoLib 4.9.3 for NeoForge/Minecraft 1.21.1 is required on both the client and server. Getting started Read installation and backups . Follow your first steps . Browse the 47-species gallery for appearances, diets, and acquisition routes. Care, research, and exploration What would you like to do? Guide Carry food and automatically feed followers Feed bags Choose comfort floor blocks and biomes for every slime Habitats and comfort Choose battle companions and elemental combos Companion combat Feed, house, capture, and transport slimes Care and capture Breed new generations and inspect traits Breeding · Genetics Discover hybrids and transformations Evolution · Advanced lineages Prepare five special lineages Ascension rituals Teach commands and organize cooperating pairs Companions and symbiosis Put your slimes to work Individual jobs · More jobs · Signals and sonar Record discoveries and build a laboratory Research and progression · Genetic research Analyze captured slimes and raise juveniles Genetic Station · Incubator Craft materials and equipment Materials and recipes Explore habitats and structures Ecosystem · Structures and altars Learn abilities and challenge bosses Combat · Bosses and minions Explore visual details Slime identities · Elemental details · Celestial appearances Reference Configuration · Balance values · Species and datapacks · Images and description · Version history"}, {"title": "Release Notes", "url": "RELEASE_NOTES.html", "text": "Release Notes Current version: 0.23.0 . Release details . See the version history for the changes in each release. 0.21.0 — Pedestal fixes, combat continuity, and rebuilt structures 0.20.1 — Creative Slime Wand 0.20.0 — Slime levels, elemental effects, and ally protection 0.19.0 — Feed bags and responsive companion combat 0.18.0 — Faster followers, flight, recovery, and habitat reference 0.17.0 — Companion skills and stronger boss encounters 0.16.0 — Companion combat postures and five followers 0.15.0 — A Slimepedia for every new player 0.14.2 — A dedicated public guide 0.14.1 — Online guide and panoramic banner 0.14.0 — Eight renewed visual identities 0.13.0 — Four signal and display jobs 0.12.0 — Structures, ascension, and more jobs 0.11.0 — Animated elemental materials 0.10.0 — Celestial appearances and lunar phases 0.9.0 — The first individual jobs 0.8.0 — Training and symbiosis 0.7.3 — SolarPunk interfaces 0.7.2 — Dimensional machines and nests 0.7.1 — A book you can hold 0.7.0 — The catalog reaches 47 species 0.6.0 — Refined elemental anatomy 0.5.0 — Elemental details and boss encounters 0.4.0 — GeckoLib and SolarPunk presentation 0.3.0 — Expanded boss patterns 0.2.0-visual.4 — Droplet bodies and elemental effects 0.2.0-visual.3 — Command-summoned boss fix 0.2.0-visual.2 — Distinct creature anatomy 0.2.0-visual.1 — The first visual rework"}, {"title": "Advanced Hybrids and Rare Metamorphoses", "url": "guides/ADVANCED_LINEAGES.html", "text": "Advanced Hybrids and Rare Metamorphoses Slime Evolution includes 47 species, 61 breeding recipes, and 14 metamorphoses . The 26 derived species do not spawn naturally or receive spawn eggs. Their offspring inherit the same 15 genes, parent IDs, and generation as other breeding results. Advanced crosses Parents Offspring Features Fire + Water Steam Blinding veil capped at five seconds; kelp and blaze powder diet Water + Ice Glacial Aquatic Pushing, extinguishing, chilling jet; water breathing; freeze immunity; fire weakness Crystal + Electric Energized Crystal Shards, refraction, mineral defense, and limited electrical conduction Wind + Fire Volatile Flame Gusts and ignition, reduced falls, fire immunity, water damage Moss + Water Bog Alternative route; Moss + Mud remains valid Compound effects share one energy cost and cooldown. Caretakers and allies are protected. Costs apply only when part of the effect is accepted. Results can breed with their own species; there is no generic rare result for arbitrary pairs. Rare routes Route Substrate and biome Requirements Catalyst and cost Crystal → Prismatic Amethyst; Stony Peaks or Dripstone Caves Adult; age 48,000; luminosity ≥0.85; exposure 12,000 Prismatic Shard; 40 energy, +30 hunger Ancestral → Celestial Purpur; End Highlands Adult; age 96,000; stability ≥0.90; exposure 18,000 Primordial Essence; 50 energy, +35 hunger Both need a caretaker, sufficient trust, calm, hunger ≤40, comfort ≥60, and energy ≥60. Exposure advances only while loaded under correct conditions. Crouch and use the catalyst. Luminosity is recessive, requiring both alleles to meet its threshold. Prismatic retains projectiles, refraction, and mineral defense with moderately higher health and mobility. Celestial retains ancestral caretaker protection with a shorter cooldown and higher cost. Transformations preserve UUID, lineage, alleles, caretaker, age, health ratio, cooldowns, breeding protection, and mutation evidence rather than creating a clone or fully healing the slime. Additional acquired lineages Parents Result Features Electric + Wind Storm Rain cloud, dark tornado, shared-energy gusts and discharges Water + Floral Coral Branching coral structures; heals allies in water while wet Sand + Fire Glass Transparent gel, arrow refraction, brief threatened camouflage Iron + Water Ferrofluid Attracts up to eight caretaker-thrown metal items within six visible blocks Fungal + Moss Mycelium Spores heal nearby allies Venom + Magma Caustic Three-second pools apply Poison and Weakness Environmental metamorphoses These routes require 24,000 age ticks , 6,000 exposure ticks , 30 energy , and +25 hunger , in addition to general care requirements. Route Environment Catalyst / minimum expressed gene Moss → Amber Flower Forest or Sunflower Plains; moss block Honeycomb; regeneration ≥0.65 Glacial Aquatic → Abyssal Deep Cold or Deep Frozen Ocean; prismarine; fully submerged at Y ≤40 Glow ink sac; luminosity ≥0.65 Corrupted → Sculk Deep Dark; sculk Echo shard; elemental potency ≥0.70 Fire → Solar Plains, Sunflower Plains, or Desert; gold block; clear day and open sky Solar Catalyst; elemental potency ≥0.65 Luminous → Lunar Plains, Meadow, or Snowy Plains; calcite; full-moon night and open sky Amethyst shard; luminosity ≥0.65 Amber slows; Abyssal combines Darkness and Slowness; Sculk responds to enemy movement with echo pulses. Solar heals in sunlight and ignites; Lunar gives a nearby caretaker Night Vision at night. Craft Solar Catalyst with a gold ingot above, sunflower / amethyst shard / sunflower across the middle, and blaze powder below. Advanced evolutions The following three metamorphoses require 96,000 age ticks , 12,000 exposure ticks , 40 energy , and +25 hunger . Eclipse is a breeding result. Lineage Final requirements Storm → Supercell Windswept Hills or Windswept Gravelly Hills; lightning rod; thunder, open sky; wind charge; potency ≥0.90 Amber → Hive Flower Forest or Sunflower Plains; honeycomb block; honeycomb; regeneration ≥0.85 Prismatic → Aurora Frozen Peaks or Ice Spikes; blue ice; clear night, open sky; Prismatic Shard; stability ≥0.90 Solar + Lunar → Eclipse Charged Solar and New Moon Lunar; sunset ritual with Prismatic Shard Hive can produce bottled honey from a glass bottle under normal harvesting conditions: 20 energy, +10 hunger, and 6,000 recovery ticks. Up to two temporary pollinators live for 200 ticks, heal allied slimes, and disappear when their Hive is lost. Supercell, Aurora, Ancestral, Celestial, and Eclipse also require their ascension milestones . Read those before consuming catalysts. Breeding · Evolution · Boss rewards"}, {"title": "Five Ascension Lineages", "url": "guides/ASCENSION.html", "text": "Five Ascension Lineages Eclipse, Supercell, Aurora, Ancestral, and Celestial require special preparation in addition to normal care, genetics, and breeding or metamorphosis. Track individual progress in the analyzer's Evolution tab. Milestones persist through saving and capsules. Eclipse: prepare both parents Keep a calm adult Solar bound to its caretaker at trust ≥40 under open sky during clear daytime. Accumulate 600 valid sunlight ticks , about 30 loaded seconds. Completed charge survives capture; exposure pauses inside capsules. Choose a Lunar whose individual phase is New Moon . The world's changing moon does not change an individual's phase. Prepare both parents normally and keep them under open sky during world ticks 12,000–12,999 , with their shared caretaker nearby, able to see them, and carrying a Prismatic Shard . Only an accepted birth consumes the shard and solar charge. Breeding two Eclipse slimes still requires sunset, open sky, a present caretaker, and the catalyst. Supercell: channel the storm A bound adult Storm with trust ≥40 needs three distinct lightning strikes hitting a powered lightning rod within eight blocks during thunder. Repeated flashes of one strike count once. Natural and summoned lightning follow the same rod and weather checks. Then complete metamorphosis on a lightning rod in Windswept Hills or Windswept Gravelly Hills, during thunder with open sky: age 96,000 ticks , expressed elemental potency ≥0.90, and 12,000 valid exposure ticks . Use a wind charge; completion costs 40 energy and +25 hunger . Aurora: travel with Prismatic Bring the same calm, bound adult Prismatic with trust ≥40 to three distinct biome IDs . Each visit requires 600 valid ticks . Changing biomes resets the unfinished visit, while completed visits remain recorded. Complete the transformation in Frozen Peaks or Ice Spikes, on blue ice, during a clear night with open sky. Requirements: age 96,000 , stability ≥0.90, and 12,000 exposure ticks . Use a Prismatic Shard; cost 40 energy and +25 hunger . Ancestral: earn the seal Craft a Primordial Seal with one each of Royal Gel, Igneous Fragment, Prismatic Shard, Nether Star, and Ancient Tablet. The first three are boss rewards; the tablet comes from the Ancestral Chamber in the End. The recipe does not require Ancestral Essence. Bring an adult Void to End Highlands on purpur. Requirements: age 48,000 , stability ≥0.80, and 12,000 valid exposure ticks . Use the seal on the slime; cost 40 energy and +30 hunger . Using a seal on the chamber's altar summons the Primordial boss instead, consuming a separate seal. Celestial: bond, research, and observations Complete all six Ancestral research stages in the caretaker's Slimepedia: observe, feed, analyze, breed, transform, and harvest. Reach 80 trust with the chosen individual. In the Overworld, place that calm adult Ancestral on an amethyst block, under open sky without rain, with at least 60 energy. In the analyzer, press Observe in this order: Observation World time modulo 24,000 Sunset 12,000–12,999 Midnight 17,500–18,499 Dawn 23,000–23,999 Each accepted observation costs 4 energy and +2 hunger . Repeating the same window does not advance the next observation. They need not occur on the same day. Capsule previews cannot perform observations. Finally, complete metamorphosis in End Highlands on purpur: age 96,000 , stability ≥0.90, 18,000 valid exposure ticks , and a Primordial Essence . Cost: 50 energy and +35 hunger . Evolution · Genetics"}, {"title": "Bosses and Minions", "url": "guides/BOSSES.html", "text": "Bosses and Minions Find one of the four natural arenas and use its ritual item on the central altar. Accepted rituals consume the item and reserve the altar until the boss dies. The arena needs 17×17 floor space and six clear blocks above. Difficulty must be above Peaceful, with no liquids, sufficient space, and no other loaded living boss within 96 blocks. Ground warnings, body pulses, and sounds signal attacks. Top and side pedestal clicks are accepted. If the player or their companions occupy the center, summoning looks for a free nearby arena position and never consumes the item on failure. Gelatinous King Health: 600 · Armor: 10 · Phases: 2 · Reward: 2 Royal Gel Craft a Gelatinous Crown with a Slime Core, Breeding Gel, and four gold ingots. Use it at the Royal Court altar in the Overworld. The King alternates jump impacts, summons, crosses, and rings. Hits apply Slowness I and launch targets. Phase two begins at half health and remains active even if healed. Minion Role Guard Melee attacker; applies Weakness II Healer Restores 14 King health per pulse, requiring range and line of sight Spitter Ranged attacker; applies Slowness I and Poison I The King maintains up to six minions. Prioritize healers to limit recovery. Magmatic Heart Health: 750 · Armor: 12 · Phases: 2 · Reward: 2 Igneous Fragments Craft a Magma Brazier with a Slime Core, Elemental Essence, two magma creams, and two blaze powders. Use the Elemental Sanctuary altar. Attacks include rings, eruptions, crosses, and twin eruptions. Hits ignite and apply Hunger II. Phase two begins at half health; water reduces damage. Up to four fire or magma servants provide ranged embers and pursuing bombs. Bomb explosions apply Blindness I and Hunger II without destroying terrain. Crystalline Colossus Health: 900 · Armor: 16 · Phases: 2 · Reward: 2 Prismatic Shards Craft a Crystal Sigil with a Slime Core, two Crystal Fragments, two amethyst shards, and a diamond. Use the Crystal Cavern altar. Shard barrages, waves, crosses, and rings apply Slowness III and Mining Fatigue II. Phase two starts at half health. Defense increases while preparing an attack; exploit recovery windows. Primordial Slime Health: 1,024 · Armor: 14 · Phases: 3 · Reward: 2 Primordial Essences Craft a Primordial Seal with Royal Gel, Igneous Fragment, Prismatic Shard, Nether Star, and Ancient Tablet. Use the Ancestral Chamber altar in the End; the chamber supplies the tablet. Attacks include waves, fire rings, shards, crosses, and orbital rupture. Hits apply Weakness I and Wither I; shards and orbital attacks also apply Levitation I. Phases change at two-thirds and one-third health. Up to three flying Ancestral Echoes attack at close range. Bring a companion team Version 0.17.0 increases health, armor, and damage to give teams of three to five slimes a meaningful role. Bring a tank, a support, and attackers with elemental combos. Minions can now select companions as targets, with nearby tanks attracting more attention. Boss warnings and recovery windows remain opportunities to move and attack. Caustic helps against armor, Water sets up electrical attacks, and Ancestral/Celestial protect the caretaker. Healing and shields share limits per ally. Team composition and care matter alongside follower count. See skills, costs, and combos . Preparation and rewards The interiors of rings, crosses, and orbital attacks also deal damage. Use distance beyond the outline, elevation, or cover as appropriate. Later phases increase damage, while an attack already being prepared retains its initial parameters. Rewards require a player-credited victory. Minions provide no rewards. Boss trophies support equipment, incubation, and rare metamorphoses . See balance values . Combat continuity in 0.22.0 All four bosses retain their target through obstructions lasting up to 40 loaded ticks, preventing brief visibility changes from repeatedly resetting attack preparation. Hits retain their normal visibility and geometry checks. Visible bonded companions can also become targets while their caretaker is alive, in Survival, and within 16 blocks of the arena centre. A boss displaced beyond the inner boundary attempts to return to the arena. After 100 loaded ticks without returning, it searches for a loaded, unoccupied position in the central area without overlapping entities, restoring health, or editing terrain. Creative players, explicit NoAI, and finite minion reservations retain their normal behaviour."}, {"title": "Breeding, Growth, and Inspection", "url": "guides/BREEDING.html", "text": "Breeding, Growth, and Inspection Breed compatible adults to produce offspring with inherited genetics. The 47 species use 61 breeding pairs , including 14 cross-species combinations. Prepare the parents Manually feed two compatible adults, binding both to the same caretaker. Required trust is 20 for docile, 40 for neutral, and 70 for hostile species. Feeders maintain hunger but do not increase trust. Each adult needs hunger at most 40, comfort and energy at least 60, and at least half health. Combat, recent damage, breeding recovery, leashes, mounts, or passengers prevent breeding. The caretaker uses Breeding Gel on each parent. A successful preparation consumes one gel in Survival and lasts 1,200 ticks , normally 60 seconds. Repeated clicks while ready neither consume more gel nor extend readiness. Invalid attempts do not consume it. Keep the parents within four blocks and clear line of sight. The server checks for solid, dry, unoccupied ground near their midpoint. Parents do not automatically seek partners. Parent order does not matter. Parent–offspring, sibling, and half-sibling pairings are rejected. The record stores both parent UUIDs and generation; more distant ancestry is not detected. See all breeding combinations . The default population cap is 12 loaded living slimes in a 32-block region around the birth, including parents and other species. This uses a spatial box. Birth and recovery A successful birth creates one individual with a new UUID, inherited genome, parent IDs, and one generation above the higher parental generation. It inherits the caretaker and starts at size 1, hunger 60, comfort 60, trust 20, and energy 70. Juveniles do not deal contact damage. Parental metamorphosis history and exposure are not inherited. Only after the server accepts the child do both parents spend 30 energy , gain 30 hunger , and begin recovery. Base recovery is 6,000 ticks , multiplied by 1.25 - 0.5 × fertility : normally 3 minutes 45 seconds to 6 minutes 15 seconds. Blocked space, incompatibility, population limits, or another mod canceling entity insertion do not apply birth costs or recovery. Parents remain ready until their timer expires. Preparation gel is not refunded; expiration does not create offspring. Growth and persistence Base growth takes 12,000 loaded ticks , ten minutes under suitable conditions. It advances once per second while hunger is below 80, comfort at least 40, and energy at least 20. Growth that increases size also requires space. Chronological age and growth progress are separate counters. The size gene determines adult size within species limits. A size-1 adult is still an adult. Size changes preserve health ratio. Genome, parents, generation, life stage, progress, and recovery persist through saves and capsules. Captured or unloaded individuals do not advance their growth or timers. Older individuals without growth fields load as generation-zero adults, preserving identity and genetics. Genetic Analyzer Use slimeevolution:genetic_analyzer on a reachable, visible slime to inspect species, generation, UUID, parents, ability, health, size, stage, age, needs, growth, recovery, and readiness. The 15 genes show both alleles and their expression. Scroll or use arrows; tooltips explain expression and genes without active gameplay effects. Inspection neither edits the slime nor consumes the analyzer. Losing the slime, line of sight, or eight-block access closes the menu. The Evolution tab shows transformation history and environmental requirements. Recipes Breeding Gel: wheat (W), glow berries (B), slimeball (S). .W. BSB .W. Genetic Analyzer: iron ingots (I), glass (G), slimeball (S). .IG ISI .I. Both recipes unlock after obtaining a slimeball and produce one item. Server settings Setting in [breeding] Default Range / purpose enabled true Player-initiated breeding localPopulationLimit 12 2–64 loaded slimes recoveryTicks 6000 200–240000; adjusted by fertility growthTicks 12000 200–240000; new juveniles mutationChance 0.02 0–0.25 per allele; affected by stability mutationStep 0.1 0–0.25 maximum allele change Existing juveniles and active recovery retain their stored durations. Timings assume 20 ticks per second and do not advance while unloaded. Mutation Stabilizer Apply a stabilizer to an eligible parent in your care before Breeding Gel. One unit protects the pair's next accepted birth against new mutations without changing inherited alleles or bypassing breeding conditions. Protection persists through saves, capsules, failed births, and readiness expiration. An accepted birth consumes protection from treated parents; offspring do not inherit it. Eclipse requires its additional solar and lunar ritual . See genetics , materials , and advanced lineages ."}, {"title": "Care and Capture", "url": "guides/CARE.html", "text": "Care and Capture Species and diets · Breeding · Companions Feeding and needs Use a food from the species' diet directly on a slime. An accepted meal consumes one item in Survival, reduces hunger by 20, and restores 10 energy. The slime must have at least 20 hunger and wait five seconds between meals. Crouch and interact with an empty hand to inspect needs. Values range from 0 to 100: low hunger is good; high energy, comfort, and trust are good. Metabolism and habitat affect hunger and energy recovery. Caretaker and trust The first player to feed a slime manually becomes its caretaker. Other players may feed it, but do not take over the bond. Temperament Trust per meal from caretaker Trust required for capture Docile 20 20 Neutral 15 40 Hostile 10 70 Hostile slimes stop selecting their caretaker as a target at 20 trust. Bonded slimes reject damage attributed to their own caretaker or another slime with the same caretaker, including melee, projectiles, explosions, thorns, and indirect magic, without losing trust, absorption, or energy, retaliating, or starting a capture cooldown. Harmful caretaker and allied slime effects are rejected before poison or wither can deal delayed damage; healing and beneficial effects still work. This protection applies at any trust level and in every order. Other players, monsters, and unattributed environmental hazards such as lava and block fire can still hurt them. All mod slime species, wild or bonded, are immune to fall damage. A bond supports care and capture; training unlocks commands and cooperation. Enclosures Choose from the floor blocks and preferred biomes for all 47 species . Each species card in the gallery also lists its preferences. The slime must stand on an accepted block: nearby blocks and walls do not count. Any accepted floor grants +35 comfort, while a preferred biome grants +30, added to a base target of 30. This gives 65 with the floor alone or 95 with both, before penalties. Different accepted blocks do not stack. Comfort adjusts by up to two points per loaded second. Avoid overcrowding: more than eight evolution slimes in the local four-block check, including the slime itself, reduces the target by 20. Fire-immune species suffer a comfort penalty in water, rain, or bubbles; freezing-immune species suffer one while burning. Build barriers and roofs appropriate to the species. Habitat tags can be changed with datapacks . Feeder The Feeder has nine slots and supports hoppers. Every two seconds it tries to feed a hungry slime within four blocks and clear line of sight, using compatible food and respecting the individual's meal cooldown. It neither assigns a caretaker nor increases trust. Its reservoir and tray face you when placed. Portable feeding Use a feed bag to carry food for your own slimes in Follow within sixteen blocks. The Royal version has five slots; upgrade it with an Igneous Fragment for fifteen. Bags use each species' diet and the normal five-second meal cooldown, without granting automatic trust. Capsules Use an empty capsule on a size-1 or size-2 slime with sufficient caretaker trust, at least half health and 10 energy, no combat or damage in the last five seconds, and no leash, mount, or passengers. Only the caretaker can capture and release it. Use an occupied capsule on solid, dry ground with free space. A rejected release keeps the slime in its capsule. Bosses and minions cannot be captured. Capsules preserve identity, genes, health, age, trust, and cooldowns. The individual is suspended while captured. Losing its occupied capsule makes it inaccessible through normal gameplay. Captures belong to their original world: back up the entire world . Recipes unlock after obtaining a slimeball. A second capsule recipe uses one Slime Core and one glass block . See materials ."}, {"title": "Celestial Appearances and Lunar Phases", "url": "guides/CELESTIAL_VISUALS.html", "text": "Celestial Appearances and Lunar Phases Eclipse has a spherical aura and two celestial bodies orbiting above it. Ferrofluid wears a covering of small spikes. Steam releases smoke from its crown, shoulders, and sides, rising and dissipating. Lunar's eight moons Each Lunar is born with one of eight individual phases. Its moon floats and gently orbits above its head. The phase persists through saving and capsule transport and does not follow the world's calendar. It also determines the Lunar job's benefit . Value Phase 0 Full moon 1 Waning gibbous 2 Last quarter 3 Waning crescent 4 New moon 5 Waxing crescent 6 First quarter 7 Waxing gibbous Summon for comparison With commands enabled: /summon slimeevolution:evolution_slime ~ ~ ~ {Species:\"slimeevolution:lunar\"} To select a phase, add LunarPhase from 0 to 7. For a new moon: /summon slimeevolution:evolution_slime ~ ~ ~ {Species:\"slimeevolution:lunar\",LunarPhase:4} Other species IDs include slimeevolution:eclipse , slimeevolution:ferrofluid , and slimeevolution:steam . Substitute the Species value in the first command."}, {"title": "Combat and Abilities", "url": "guides/COMBAT.html", "text": "Combat and Abilities Bonded companions in 0.17.0 Bonded slimes use the new 47-species companion combat system . It defines their roles, attacks, support, energy, and recovery. The ecological examples below describe wild species and general elemental traits. Companion-specific rules take precedence for bonded slimes. Activation requirements Offensive slime abilities require an adult, a valid target, sufficient energy, and an available cooldown. Physical contact must be accepted before contact effects apply. Juveniles do not deal contact damage. Genes affect strength, duration, regeneration, and defense. Species values are baselines; individuals may perform differently. Inspect the slime you are raising with the analyzer. Main effects Group Examples Mobility and knockback Common attacks with jumps; Water pushes and extinguishes; Wind creates gusts. All mod slime species are immune to fall damage Fire and cold Fire ignites; Ice chills and extinguishes burning targets; Magma recovers in lava Recovery Moss and Floral regenerate under favorable conditions; Fungal benefits from nearby mushrooms Control Mud slows; Sand blinds; Fungal weakens; Venom leaves a toxic cloud Mineral defense Stone, Iron, and Obsidian offer different impact defenses Crystals and electricity Crystal fires shards; Electric can chain discharges through wet targets; Amethyst reveals threats Dimensional forms End teleports away; Void pulls threats; Ancestral protects an injured caretaker Browse all 47 species in the gallery . Hybrids and metamorphoses have their own ability, cost, and cooldown combinations. Elemental reactions Water, rain, and bubbles hinder Fire's ignition, and Fire takes damage when wet. Ice extinguishes burning targets, resists freezing, and is vulnerable to fire. Electrical discharges are stronger against wet targets and have limited propagation. Suitable terrain supports regeneration, resonance, and magmatic recovery. Line of sight, allies, caretaker relationships, and target conditions are checked. Damage, healing, status, and knockback cancellations preserve their respective protections. Slime abilities do not alter terrain. Energy and configuration Valid activations use the species' energy cost and cooldown. Passive defenses follow their own conditions. Hunger and comfort influence energy recovery: maintain a suitable habitat . Server settings control abilities, costs, damage, duration, sounds, and particles. Bosses have separate patterns, contact effects, and summons; see balance values ."}, {"title": "Companions, Levels, and Symbiosis", "url": "guides/COMPANIONS.html", "text": "Companions, Levels, and Symbiosis Open the companion panel Manually feed a slime to become its caretaker. Then crouch and use the Genetic Analyzer on your slime . Normal analyzer use still opens genetic inspection. Control requires a nearby caretaker, clear line of sight, and building permission. Levels and commands Levels 1–10 replace practice lessons. Eating a suitable food grants 2 XP; kills grant 8 XP for passive mobs, 20 for hostiles, and 160 for bosses. Each level improves health, armor, and damage without changing genes. Command Minimum level Behavior Free 1 Resume natural movement and feeding Wait 1 Hold the current position Follow 1 Follow the caretaker in the same dimension Return home 1 Return to the marked home and wait Commands require 40 trust; Free remains available below that value. Mark a home before returning. Feed bags can feed slimes in Follow. Follow uses faster hops and more frequent path updates outside combat, helping slower species keep up. Ancestral and Celestial fly in a small formation while following; they use collision-aware air navigation and return to ground movement when the order ends or combat interrupts it. All mod slime species are immune to fall damage, including wild individuals and those without wings. Bonded slimes also reject damage and harmful effects attributed to their own caretaker; see care and capture . A loaded follower more than 32 blocks away can teleport to a safe, dry, supported point near its caretaker in the same dimension . Attempts run at most once per loaded second, with a five-second cooldown after success. It checks space for the whole slime, hazards, and the world border. No teleport occurs during combat, recent attacks, defeat, immobilization, riding, or leashing. If there is no safe point, it continues trying to follow normally. No chunks are forced to load, and other dimensions or an unavailable caretaker do not trigger a teleport. Energy limits special skills rather than learned movement or basic attacks. Even at zero energy, companions can follow, fly, and reacquire hostiles in Aggressive. Ranged attackers that cannot afford their next skill approach for a basic melee attack. Feed and care for the team so its special skills recover; the five-follower limit remains shared across dimensions. Defeated companions A bonded slime that takes lethal ordinary damage enters a defeated state for 10 loaded seconds , with three stars orbiting above its head. It remains in place, stops attacking, casting, flying, and working, and cannot be captured during recovery. Enemies cannot damage it further during this period, and boss minions switch to other targets. It then gets up with 50% health , at least 20 energy, and two seconds of protection against immediate defeat. Its identity, genes, trust, level, XP, commands, follower reservation, and stored belongings remain intact. No loot, experience, or duplicate slime is created. Existing skill recoveries continue normally. The timer is saved and pauses while unloaded. Wild slimes retain normal death. Administrative removal and damage that bypasses invulnerability, including the void, keep their normal behavior. Combat postures Choose a combat posture independently of Free, Wait, Follow, and Return home: Posture Behavior Passive Does not automatically attack or retaliate, even if the caretaker or slime is hit. Defensive Default for new and existing individuals. Defends itself and its caretaker and assists against the caretaker's recent attack target. Aggressive Includes Defensive behavior and seeks visible hostile mobs within a spherical 16-block radius. Automatic basic combat requires adulthood and at least 40 trust. Special skills require their listed energy cost. Passive remains selectable at low trust. It also prevents offensive ability effects; supportive abilities and ordinary care remain available. The caretaker, bonded slimes, tame animals, allies, spectators, Creative players, and PvP-protected players are not valid targets. Priority goes to the caretaker's recent attacker, then the slime's attacker, then the caretaker's recent victim. Combat records expire after 200 ticks, normally ten seconds. Targets are rechecked for range, sight, and eligibility; movement orders resume after combat. Waiting guards stay within eight blocks of their anchor. Followers do not pursue targets farther than 32 blocks from their caretaker, in addition to their local 16-block combat range. Return home can pause for local combat, bounded to 16 blocks from its starting point; the return resumes afterward. Postures persist through saves, capsules, and metamorphoses. Offspring start Defensive rather than inheriting their parents' selected posture. Five followers per caretaker At most five slimes may be in Follow for one caretaker across the whole world , including all dimensions. A sixth request is rejected without changing the previous order. Hover over Follow for the reserved follower count. Unloaded slimes keep their reserved slot. Free, Wait, Return home, capture, or removal releases it. Releasing a captured follower restores Follow if there is room; with five occupied slots, the released slime switches to Wait at its release location, keeping its posture, level, and XP. Old worlds with more than five followers move excess individuals to Wait as they load. Reservations are stored in data/slimeevolution_followers.dat ; include it in complete world backups. Mark a home Mark home here uses the caretaker's current position. Choose solid, dry ground inside the world border with room for the entire slime. A home can be marked before learning Return home. Return requires the same dimension and a loaded, unblocked location. Enable symbiosis Open each partner's panel and enable cooperation. Both must be adults with the same caretaker , within six blocks and mutual line of sight, calm, with trust ≥40, energy ≥30, hunger ≤60, and comfort ≥40. Recent damage, breeding, leashes, mounts, or passengers prevent cooperation. Partners cooperate while Free or Waiting. Follow and Return home suspend work. Cooperation starts disabled for new and existing individuals. Partners Work Cost per participant Shared recovery Water + Moss Advance one compatible crop by one growth stage 6 energy, +3 hunger 400 ticks / 20 seconds Electric + Iron Add up to four processing ticks to a station or incubator 2 energy, +1 hunger 20 ticks / 1 second No valid work means no charge. Both participants receive recovery, preventing immediate reuse in another pair. Water + Moss Keep partners within four blocks of crops and clear line of sight. Wheat, carrots, potatoes, beetroot, and other compatible CropBlock plants are supported. Cooperation does not plant or harvest. The caretaker must be online in the same dimension with permission to alter the location. Work respects mobGriefing and NeoForge protection events. Electric + Iron Keep partners within four blocks of the machine, with clear line of sight. The capsule must belong to their caretaker. Assistance occurs only after the machine accepts a valid processing tick; it reduces processing time without bypassing ingredients or changing results, genes, growth rewards, identities, or token rules. Persistence and settings Level, XP, commands, home, cooperation preferences, and recovery persist through saves, capsules, and metamorphoses. Recovery pauses while captured or unloaded. Offspring start at level 1 with no XP and do not inherit commands or homes. Server options companions.training and companions.symbiosis can pause these features without deleting progress. Canceling commands and disabling cooperation remain available. See individual jobs . Skills and team roles All 47 companion species now have tiered attacks or support skills. See the complete combat catalog for roles, costs, cooldowns, combos, and boss team suggestions. Carry food for your team The Royal and Magmatic Feed Bags store five or fifteen food stacks. Carry one to automatically feed only your own following slimes within sixteen blocks."}, {"title": "Companion Combat", "url": "guides/COMPANION_COMBAT.html", "text": "Companion Combat Individual levels scale both basic attack and offensive skill damage: level 1 uses this page's base values; level 10 deals 2.62× damage and also has 2.8× health and +9 armor. Caretakers and slimes with the same caretaker cannot harm their own bonded slimes. Attacks use animated fire, water, frost, storm, venom, solar, earth, and arcane textures. Projectiles have luminous cores and tapered trails; impacts use expanding rings, with richer high-rarity sigils. Reduced motion and visual quality options limit animations. Player guide · Bond and commands · Bosses In 0.17.0, all 47 species receive a companion combat profile based on acquisition difficulty. Starter species use affordable attacks; hybrids and advanced lineages add combos, control, and range. Prismatic, Supercell, Aurora, Eclipse, and Ancestral provide rare tools. Celestial occupies the final tier with powerful offense and protection, a long windup, and a high energy cost. Prepare your team Use adults bonded to the same caretaker, with at least 40 trust. Special skills require their listed energy cost; following and basic attacks still work at zero energy. Feed and care for the group before a ritual. Defensive responds to attacks received or made by the caretaker; Aggressive also seeks visible hostiles within 16 blocks. Passive retains support and protection while cancelling attacks, including projectiles already in flight. Follow requires training 40 and remains limited to five slimes per caretaker. Tanks close in and attract more attention from nearby minions. Ranged attackers try to maintain distance; supports position around the caretaker or an injured ally. Companions try to move away from boss warning centers when safe ground is available. This does not guarantee a dodge: respect each attack's geometry and avoid trapping your slimes against walls. For three to five companions, start with one tank, one support, and one to three attackers , including an elemental combo. Stone, Floral, Water, and Electric make an accessible team; replace roles with advanced lineages as you progress. Combos and limits Water + electricity: Soaked lasts about five seconds. Electric, Storm, and Energized Crystal deal 50% more primary damage to wet targets. Chains have bounded target counts, range, and line-of-sight checks. Ice: three Chilled applications briefly root a target, followed by six seconds of shared freeze protection. Natural immunities still apply. Caustic: creates a short corrosion field that removes four armor points. Multiple casters cannot stack the armor reduction indefinitely. Eclipse: alternates solar and lunar phases. Landing the lunar phase on the same target before its solar mark expires triggers an area convergence. Healing: each ally accepts only one companion heal every two seconds, capped at six health per activation even with increased server settings. Shields: Ancestral grants four absorption health; Celestial grants eight. Shields last five seconds, with a shared ten-second renewal lock. Multiple slimes cannot stack them. Control: pulls and pushes respect knockback resistance; resistant bosses cannot be held in an endless tornado. Attacks check range, sight, and allies. Projectiles can miss and walls block them. Interrupted windups cost no energy; launched shots cost energy even if they miss. Capture and world reload preserve recovery without replaying pending casts. These attacks do not destroy blocks. All 47 species Base values assume 20 ticks per second, before genes, armor, effects, and server settings. Damage is the primary special hit; areas, ongoing effects, fire, and contact are additional where described. Zero denotes support. Support range describes its assistance radius; species conditions still apply. Hover over the companion portrait to inspect its profile. Wild slimes retain their separate ecological abilities. Species Tier / role Ability Damage Energy Cooldown (s) Range Common Slime 1 / Brawler Impact Jump 3 4 3 2.5 Water Slime 1 / Ranged Soaking Jet 2 5 3 7 Stone Slime 1 / Tank Stone Charge 4 6 5 5 Mud Slime 1 / Brawler Muddy Impact 2 4 3.5 3 Sand Slime 1 / Skirmisher Sand Burst 2 5 4.5 4 Fungal Slime 1 / Support Weakening Spores 2 5 5 4 Moss Slime 1 / Support Moss Recovery 0 3 5 5 Wind Slime 1 / Skirmisher Wind Gust 2 5 4 5 Fire Slime 2 / Ranged Ember Spit 3 6 4 8 Ice Slime 2 / Ranged Frost Shard 2.5 6 4.5 8 Crystal Slime 2 / Ranged Crystal Shot 4 7 5 9 Amethyst Slime 2 / Ranged Resonance 3 7 5 8 Corrupted Slime 2 / Ranged Deterioration 4 10 7 7 Soul Slime 2 / Brawler Soul Siphon 4 8 5 4 Void Slime 2 / Skirmisher Spatial Pull 3 8 6 6 Magma Slime 2 / Tank Lava Touch 4 8 6 4 Floral Slime 2 / Support Vital Bloom 0 5 5 6 Luminous Slime 2 / Support Cave Guide 0 5 8 6 End Slime 2 / Skirmisher Dimensional Step 3 8 6 5 Iron Slime 2 / Tank Iron Guard 4 6 5 4 Obsidian Slime 2 / Tank Obsidian Bastion 5 7 7 4 Electric Slime 2 / Ranged Directed Discharge 3 8 5 7 Venom Slime 2 / Ranged Toxic Cloud 2 8 6.5 7 Energized Crystal Slime 3 / Ranged Conductive Shard 5 10 6 10 Ferrofluid Slime 3 / Ranged Magnetic Needles 5 9 5 8 Caustic Slime 3 / Ranged Corrosive Pool 2 10 7 7 Sculk Slime 3 / Ranged Echo Pulse 6 12 7 9 Bog Slime 3 / Tank Mire 4 8 5 4 Steam Slime 3 / Skirmisher Steam Veil 3 8 5 5 Glacial Aquatic Slime 3 / Ranged Glacial Jet 4 10 5.5 9 Volatile Flame Slime 3 / Skirmisher Flame Gust 5 10 5.5 7 Amber Slime 3 / Tank Adhesive Resin 3 8 5.5 5 Abyssal Slime 3 / Ranged Abyssal Lure 5 10 6.5 8 Solar Slime 3 / Ranged Solar Flare 5 10 6 9 Lunar Slime 3 / Ranged Lunar Tide 4 9 6 9 Magmatic Slime 3 / Tank Magmatic Rupture 6 10 5.5 5 Coral Slime 3 / Support Restoring Reef 0 8 6 5 Mycelium Slime 3 / Support Spore Network 0 10 7 5 Glass Slime 3 / Skirmisher Refractive Camouflage 4 8 6 6 Storm Slime 3 / Ranged Storm Front 5 12 7.5 8 Prismatic Slime 4 / Ranged Prismatic Refraction 7 16 9 11 Supercell Slime 4 / Ranged Storm Core 8 20 12 10 Aurora Slime 4 / Support Aurora Veil 0 16 10 5 Eclipse Slime 4 / Ranged Convergence 7 18 8 10 Ancestral Slime 4 / Tank Ancestral Guardian 5 18 11 6 Hive Slime 4 / Support Battle Pollinators 0 12 10 6 Celestial Slime 5 / Ranged Astral Judgment 18 28 20 12 What each skill does Common Slime — Impact Jump: Leaps into its target and delivers a knockback impact. Water Slime — Soaking Jet: Fires water, pushes and soaks its target to prepare elemental combos. Stone Slime — Stone Charge: Prepares a short charge and delivers a heavy knockback impact. Mud Slime — Muddy Impact: A close-range strike that slows its target. Sand Slime — Sand Burst: Raises sand, dealing close damage and brief Blindness. Fungal Slime — Weakening Spores: Nearby spores deal damage and weaken a small enemy group. Moss Slime — Moss Recovery: Efficiently regenerates itself while wet or standing on moss. Wind Slime — Wind Gust: Pushes a small group with a quick gust. Fire Slime — Ember Spit: Fires an aimed ember that ignites its enemy. Ice Slime — Frost Shard: Three chill applications briefly root the target, followed by temporary freeze immunity. Crystal Slime — Crystal Shot: Fires an accurate shard while keeping distance. Can refract arrows. Amethyst Slime — Resonance: A pulse that deals damage and reveals nearby enemies with Glowing. Corrupted Slime — Deterioration: Fires a corrupted fragment that applies Wither. Soul Slime — Soul Siphon: Drains and slows its target while recovering some of its own health. Void Slime — Spatial Pull: Deals damage and pulls its enemy closer. Magma Slime — Lava Touch: A close incendiary strike; recovers health in lava. Floral Slime — Vital Bloom: Directly heals its injured caretaker within six blocks. Luminous Slime — Cave Guide: Grants its caretaker Night Vision in dark caves outside combat. End Slime — Dimensional Step: Fights up close and uses a defensive blink when injured. Iron Slime — Iron Guard: Combines high armor, melee protection and a guarding impact. Obsidian Slime — Obsidian Bastion: A slow, blast-resistant tank with a heavy close impact. Electric Slime — Directed Discharge: A short-range discharge that conducts through nearby soaked enemies. Venom Slime — Toxic Cloud: Leaves a temporary poisonous area at its target. Energized Crystal Slime — Conductive Shard: Its shot conducts a discharge to another target; soaked enemies take more damage. Ferrofluid Slime — Magnetic Needles: Fires metal needles and can intercept one arrow every five seconds. Caustic Slime — Corrosive Pool: Creates a three-second pool that deals periodic damage and reduces armor by up to four points. Sculk Slime — Echo Pulse: Prepares a medium-range sonic pulse against moving targets, dealing damage and Darkness. Bog Slime — Mire: A stronger impact that spreads slowing to nearby enemies. Steam Slime — Steam Veil: A short-range steam attack that applies Blindness. Glacial Aquatic Slime — Glacial Jet: A shot that soaks, pushes and builds chill. Volatile Flame Slime — Flame Gust: Combines area knockback with fire on the primary target. Amber Slime — Adhesive Resin: A resin impact that applies strong Slowness. Abyssal Slime — Abyssal Lure: A medium-range attack combining damage, Darkness and Slowness. Solar Slime — Solar Flare: Fires solar flame and recovers its own health in sunlight. Lunar Slime — Lunar Tide: Fires a slowing lunar shard and supports its caretaker’s vision at night. Magmatic Slime — Magmatic Rupture: An advanced form with stronger incendiary impact and greater reach. Coral Slime — Restoring Reef: Stronger area healing that requires both the slime and allies to be wet. Mycelium Slime — Spore Network: Shares healing among nearby allies, prioritizing the most injured. Glass Slime — Refractive Camouflage: A close strike with brief camouflage and periodic arrow refraction. Storm Slime — Storm Front: Combines discharge, knockback and secondary damage to nearby enemies. Prismatic Slime — Prismatic Refraction: Its shot refracts into up to two nearby enemies for reduced damage. Supercell Slime — Storm Core: After a long windup, releases area lightning and leaves a tornado that groups enemies. Aurora Slime — Aurora Veil: Creates a temporary zone that protects allies and slows enemies. Eclipse Slime — Convergence: Alternates fire and slowing; completing both phases on one target releases an area convergence. Ancestral Slime — Ancestral Guardian: Grants its caretaker a finite shield during combat and repels their attacker. Hive Slime — Battle Pollinators: Two temporary pollinators alternate ally healing and weakening the marked target. Celestial Slime — Astral Judgment: Charges a powerful beam with secondary area impact. Protects the team and grants a stronger caretaker shield. Continuous combat Basic attacks continue while special skills recover. Melee keeps a one-second interval. Ranged and support slimes can fire weaker basic shots every 1.5 seconds, within eight blocks or their shorter profile range. Basic shots cost no energy and apply no special-skill effects: they use 55% of the species' basic damage, or 35% for support, with normal gene and level multipliers. Defensive companions finish an engaged fight rather than abandoning it solely because the caretaker's initial hit aged out. Aggressive companions retain a valid target instead of switching to slightly closer enemies; direct caretaker threats still take priority. Brief obstructions allow up to two seconds of pursuit, but attacks still require visibility and cannot pass through walls. Wounded bonded slimes use companion positioning instead of the automatic flight response of docile wild slimes. Territory limits, ally protection, Passive stance, and skill costs remain enforced."}, {"title": "Ecosystem and Habitats", "url": "guides/ECOSYSTEM.html", "text": "Ecosystem and Habitats Finding slimes The 21 natural species spawn in suitable environments, in darkness, outside Peaceful difficulty, and subject to space and population limits. The other 26 forms come from breeding or metamorphosis; see the species gallery . Environment Natural species examples Plains and forests Common, Moss, Wind Swamps and mangroves Mud, Venom Mushroom fields Fungal Rivers and beaches Water Frozen regions Ice Deserts Sand Caves and mineral regions Stone, Iron, Amethyst, Obsidian, Luminous Nether Fire, Magma, Soul End End, Void Specific biome permissions are configurable through datapacks . The Slimepedia records where you observed an individual, including captivity. Food and groups Hungry slimes seek loose compatible food, consuming nearby items with line of sight and respecting meal conditions. This does not establish a caretaker or trust: feed manually for a bond. Social species approach calm individuals of the same species and caretaker; the sociability gene adjusts that tendency. Territorial species defend their home region, but caretaker bonding ends territorial defense. Combat, hunger, and rest change movement priorities. Nests and colonies Surface nests feature roots, moss, and flowers around gel. Underground colonies use stones and small glowing fungi. Both introduce limited founder groups, with Overworld and Nether variants; they are not infinite slime sources. Frequency and population limits are adjustable in configuration . Special structures provide another exploration layer with materials and ritual locations. Building a habitat Provide preferred flooring and biome, space to jump, food, and limited crowding. Comfort affects recovery and breeding. House water-sensitive and fire-sensitive species appropriately. See care and capture ."}, {"title": "Elemental Materials and Details", "url": "guides/ELEMENTAL_DETAILS.html", "text": "Elemental Materials and Details Corrupted A dark coating covers the body with smoothly moving iridescent patches. Red, pink, white, and black fissures remain over the surface, following the gel's movement. Lunar Twenty craters cover its top, sides, and back, each with a pale rim and recessed shaded center. Eyes and mouth remain clear. Its floating moon preserves the individual's phase. See all eight phases and commands . Solar Rays and corona complete a rotation in 9.6 seconds . Individual rays pulse on separate timings while the warm corona texture ripples. Upper flames continue following the body. GIFs use four real frames of the same individual, ten ticks apart, displayed for half a second each. Reduced motion stops the additional decorative movements."}, {"title": "Hybrids and Metamorphoses", "url": "guides/EVOLUTION.html", "text": "Hybrids and Metamorphoses Acquire derived species by breeding compatible adults or transforming an existing individual through metamorphosis. Breeding combinations Parents, in either order Offspring Crystal + Electric Energized Crystal Electric + Wind Storm Fire + Water Steam Fungal + Moss Mycelium Iron + Water Ferrofluid Moss + Mud Bog Moss + Water Bog Sand + Fire Glass Solar + Lunar Eclipse Stone + Fire Magmatic Venom + Magma Caustic Water + Floral Coral Water + Ice Glacial Aquatic Wind + Fire Volatile Flame All 47 species can also breed with their own species, for 61 total pairs . Parents must satisfy care, relatedness, energy, and space requirements . Offspring inherit alleles; their species follows the defined recipe rather than arbitrary ability mixing. Metamorphoses Source → result Catalyst Substrate Minimum expressed gene Amber → Hive Honeycomb Honeycomb block Regeneration ≥ 0.85 Ancestral → Celestial Primordial Essence Purpur block Stability ≥ 0.90 Corrupted → Sculk Echo shard Sculk Elemental potency ≥ 0.70 Crystal → Prismatic Prismatic Shard Amethyst block Luminosity ≥ 0.85 Fire → Magmatic Magma cream Magma block Elemental potency ≥ 0.60 Fire → Solar Solar Catalyst Gold block Elemental potency ≥ 0.65 Glacial Aquatic → Abyssal Glow ink sac Prismarine Luminosity ≥ 0.65 Luminous → Lunar Amethyst shard Calcite Luminosity ≥ 0.65 Moss → Amber Honeycomb Moss block Regeneration ≥ 0.65 Moss → Floral Sunflower Moss block Regeneration ≥ 0.50 Prismatic → Aurora Prismatic Shard Blue ice Stability ≥ 0.90 Stone → Crystal Amethyst shard Amethyst block Resistance ≥ 0.60 Storm → Supercell Wind charge Lightning rod Elemental potency ≥ 0.90 Void → Ancestral Primordial Seal Purpur block Stability ≥ 0.80 Open Evolution in the analyzer for biome, temperature, time, weather, depth, age, accumulated exposure, and other route requirements. Early routes require 12,000 age ticks and 6,000 exposure ticks; advanced routes require longer preparation. See advanced lineages for the full route details. The adult must be bound to its caretaker, sufficiently trusting, calm, at hunger ≤40, comfort and energy ≥60, and at least half health, without combat or breeding readiness. It must meet the recipe's gene, substrate, biome, temperature, and environmental requirements. Solar requires clear daytime with open sky. Lunar requires a full-moon night with open sky. Abyssal requires full submersion at Y ≤40. Supercell requires thunder and open sky; Aurora requires a clear night with open sky. Exposure advances only while loaded under valid conditions. It pauses outside those conditions, in capsules, or in unloaded chunks. Complete a transformation As the caretaker, crouch and use the catalyst after meeting every requirement. Completion consumes the item and applies the recipe's energy and hunger costs. The slime preserves identity, alleles, caretaker, ancestry, age, and history. A metamorphosis changes that individual; breeding creates a new child. Completed caretaker actions are recorded in the Slimepedia. Eclipse, Supercell, Aurora, Ancestral, and Celestial also require ascension milestones . Recipes and validation are documented under datapacks ."}, {"title": "Feed Bags", "url": "guides/FEED_BAGS.html", "text": "Feed Bags Player guide · Care and capture · Companions · Species and diets Carry slime food in a dedicated bag to automatically feed your own companions in Follow , within a sixteen-block sphere around you in the same dimension. Use the bag to open its inventory. It works from your main inventory, hotbar, or offhand; a bag left in a chest or dropped on the ground does not feed slimes. Royal Feed Bag — five slots Craft with one Royal Gel from the Gelatinous King, three Leather , and two String : S . S L G L . L . S = String, L = Leather, G = Royal Gel, . = empty. This produces one Royal Feed Bag with five slots , each using the food's normal stack limit. Magmatic Feed Bag — fifteen slots Combine one Royal Feed Bag with one Igneous Fragment from the Magmatic Heart in a crafting grid. Their positions do not matter. The upgrade consumes both ingredients and creates one Magmatic Feed Bag with fifteen slots . Its existing food, slot positions, and custom name are preserved. What goes inside The bag accepts items used in at least one slime species' diet, including items such as minerals that players cannot eat. Each follower still eats only its own species diet . For example, an Ancestral accepts Golden Carrots or Glistering Melon Slices, not Apples. Bags and other item containers cannot be nested inside it. Automatic meals Once per loaded second, the bag checks your loaded, living followers inside sixteen blocks, prioritizing the hungriest. It skips other players' slimes, wild slimes, Free/Wait/Return home, defeated individuals, and slimes that are not hungry. Follow must remain enabled and the slime must retain the trust required to obey its command. A successful meal consumes one compatible item , reduces hunger by 20 , restores 10 energy , and starts the slime's normal five-second meal cooldown . It does not assign a caretaker or increase trust. Multiple bags cannot bypass the individual cooldown. Contents stay on the bag item when you close it, transfer it, save the world, or upgrade it. Automatic feeding also works while the bag is open, with the visible item counts updating normally. Energy is required for special skills and jobs. It no longer freezes learned movement or basic combat: hungry followers can still follow and respond to their combat posture while waiting for food and skill recovery."}, {"title": "Genetic Research", "url": "guides/GENETIC_RESEARCH.html", "text": "Genetic Research The Slimepedia records observed expression bands and genes with verified changes at birth. An unusual trait alone does not prove a mutation. Discover variants Analyze a reachable, visible live slime or complete a valid capsule analysis at a Genetic Station. The Slimepedia's Genes tab accumulates expression bands observed in analyzed members of that species. Band Calculated gene expression Low 0 through 0.25, inclusive Intermediate Above 0.25 and below 0.75 High 0.75 through 1, inclusive Expression respects additive, dominant, or recessive rules. Gameplay effects still follow species rules. The bands apply to all 15 existing genes and accumulate per species and player. Repeating the same analysis does not inflate counts. Storage holds up to three bands per gene rather than an expanding list of genomes or UUIDs. Observation, feeding, and witnessing births unlock their own facts; genetic findings require analysis. Books show their current reader's progress. Spectators do not advance research. Verified birth mutations Inheritance records genes where at least one allele actually changed after mutation and clamping. Zero-step, zero-delta, or clamped unchanged results do not register false mutations. A real allele change can occur even if the average additive expression stays the same. After analyzing a descendant, the journal distinguishes: Verified mutations: genes changed in analyzed births with recorded provenance. Birth without new changes: a known birth record with no new allele changes. Unavailable history: a descendant without verifiable birth provenance. Founder variation and inherited parental alleles are not evidence of a new mutation in that child. Findings concern the individual's direct birth, not a reconstruction of every ancestor. Hover over genes in the analyzer for provenance, expression, and gameplay effect details. Persistence and compatibility BirthMutationsKnown and BirthMutationGenes store bounded birth evidence using stable gene enum names. Missing or invalid history loads as unavailable; old saves are not retroactively assigned mutations based on rare values. Evidence persists through capsules, station readings, incubation, and metamorphosis. Incubation cannot modify genome, lineage, or birth evidence. A changed birth record invalidates an open inspection. Older journals retain species, stages, and routes; new analysis fills missing findings. Invalid optional genetic data is discarded without erasing other valid facts. Journals are shared across dimensions by player UUID. The current journal schema is 4 as of version 0.15.0, which also stores first-login book delivery. The server sends only the player's discoveries and selected species details. Client and server must use matching mod versions."}, {"title": "Genetic Station", "url": "guides/GENETIC_STATION.html", "text": "Genetic Station Analyze a captured individual without releasing it. The handheld analyzer remains available for live slimes. Recipe I G I R A R I I I I = iron ingot; G = glass; R = redstone; A = Genetic Analyzer. Item ID: slimeevolution:genetic_station . Operation Insert an occupied capsule in the first slot. Insert paper and redstone in the following slots. As the individual's caretaker, press Analyze . After 100 loaded ticks , press View genes . Remove the capsule to transport or release the slime. Analysis consumes one paper and one redstone only on completion . At 20 ticks per second, a cycle takes five seconds. Removing ingredients pauses progress; replacing them resumes it. Changing or removing the individual cancels without charging. Inserting items alone does not start work. The completed reading remains available while the same valid capsule stays in the station; reopening it does not charge again. A new analysis session requires ingredients after the capsule is removed and that removal is processed. Research remains in the player's Slimepedia. The inspection shows captured health, needs, age, alleles, lineage, and evolution progress. The slime does not age, eat, breed, or mutate in the station. Removing the capsule, losing block access, or leaving range closes the inspection. The monitor animates during processing and stops when paused or complete. Research and progression · Capsules"}, {"title": "Getting Started", "url": "guides/GETTING_STARTED.html", "text": "Getting Started 1. Find your first slime Explore the habitats in the species gallery . Natural slimes spawn in darkness, in suitable biomes, and outside Peaceful difficulty. Moss, Water, Fungal, and Luminous are docile; other species may retaliate or defend their territory. Check the diet before preparing an enclosure. Common accepts apples, wheat, and slimeballs; Moss accepts moss blocks and glow berries. 2. Feed and earn trust Use a compatible food directly on a hungry slime. Its first manual feeding establishes its caretaker. Keep feeding it when hungry; rejected meals do not consume food. Crouch and interact with an empty hand to inspect its needs. Low hunger and high energy, comfort, and trust support a healthy slime. See care and capture . 3. Build an enclosure Choose suitable flooring and barriers that contain jumps. Avoid overcrowding and keep Fire away from water. A Feeder holds nine stacks and feeds nearby compatible slimes, but trust must be earned through manual feeding. 4. Capture and transport Once trust is sufficient, use an empty capsule on a calm size-1 or size-2 slime with at least half health and 10 energy. Only its caretaker may capture and release it. Release it onto solid, dry ground with room for its full body. 5. Record discoveries Use the Slimepedia on a nearby slime to record its species; use it in the air to open your journal. Feeding, analysis, births, and transformations unlock additional research independently. In version 0.15.0, each player receives one Slimepedia on their first login to a world. Delivery does not repeat after death or reconnection. With a full inventory, the book drops at your feet. Existing worlds receive this delivery on the first login after updating, unless the player already carries a book. Craft a replacement with one book and one slimeball . 6. Develop your collection Craft a Genetic Analyzer , research individuals, breed compatible adults , and discover metamorphoses . Train companions , set up jobs , and prepare for boss encounters . Version 0.15.0 adds 16 Minecraft advancements. Open the Advancements screen with L by default and select Slime Evolution."}, {"title": "Habitats and Comfort", "url": "guides/HABITATS.html", "text": "Habitats and Comfort Player guide · Care and capture · Species gallery Use this list to choose a floor for each of the 47 slime species . These are the default comfort preferences, including inherited habitat blocks for hybrids. The gallery also shows the floor and biomes on each species card. Preferred biomes improve comfort; they do not imply that an acquired species spawns there naturally. How comfort works The slime must stand on a listed block . Placing that block nearby or in a wall does not grant the floor bonus. Any one accepted block gives the same bonus; combining several types does not stack it. Other block variants count only if listed. Water, food, decorations, and light do not provide a general comfort bonus. Environment Comfort target before penalties Neither preferred floor nor preferred biome 30 Preferred biome only 60 Preferred floor only 65 Preferred floor and preferred biome 95 Comfort moves toward this target by up to two points per loaded second . Keep the slime in its enclosure while it adjusts. Crouch and interact with an empty hand to check its current needs. More than eight evolution slimes in the local four-block check subtracts 20 from the target; the slime itself counts. A fire-immune slime in water, rain, or bubbles, or a freezing-immune slime on fire, receives a 50-point penalty. The final environmental target is clamped to 0–100. For example, Ancestral standing on Purpur Block , End Stone Bricks , or Block of Gold tends toward 65 comfort. In End Highlands , that becomes 95 before penalties. Mixing those three floors provides no additional bonus. Floors and biomes for all species Names follow Minecraft 1.21.1 in English. Server datapacks can change both the block tags and species biome preferences; this table lists the mod defaults. Species Accepted comfort floor blocks Preferred comfort biomes Abyssal Slime Prismarine, Dark Prismarine, Blue Ice Deep Cold Ocean, Deep Frozen Ocean Amber Slime Moss Block, Honeycomb Block Flower Forest, Sunflower Plains Amethyst Slime Block of Amethyst, Calcite, Smooth Basalt Lush Caves, Deep Dark Ancestral Slime Purpur Block, End Stone Bricks, Block of Gold End Highlands Aurora Slime Blue Ice, Packed Ice, Block of Amethyst Frozen Peaks, Ice Spikes Bog Slime Mud, Moss Block, Clay Swamp, Mangrove Swamp Caustic Slime Mud, Mycelium, Podzol, Magma Block, Basalt, Blackstone Swamp Celestial Slime Purpur Block, End Stone Bricks, Block of Gold End Highlands Common Slime Grass Block, Moss Block, Slime Block Plains, Sunflower Plains Coral Slime Prismarine, Brain Coral Block, Tube Coral Block, Bubble Coral Block Warm Ocean Corrupted Slime Sculk, Deepslate, Mossy Cobblestone Deep Dark Crystal Slime Block of Amethyst, Calcite, Stone Stony Peaks, Dripstone Caves Eclipse Slime End Stone, Purpur Block, Obsidian End Highlands Electric Slime Stone, Block of Copper, Sand Stony Shore, Savanna End Slime End Stone, End Stone Bricks, Purpur Block End Highlands, End Midlands Energized Crystal Slime Block of Amethyst, Calcite, Stone Stony Peaks, Dripstone Caves Ferrofluid Slime Block of Iron, Block of Copper, Block of Raw Iron Stony Shore Fire Slime Magma Block, Netherrack, Basalt Nether Wastes, Basalt Deltas, Badlands Floral Slime Moss Block, Grass Block, Flowering Azalea Forest, Lush Caves Fungal Slime Mycelium, Podzol, Brown Mushroom Block Mushroom Fields Glacial Aquatic Slime Ice, Packed Ice, Snow Block Frozen River, Frozen Ocean Glass Slime Sand, Glass, Tinted Glass Desert Hive Slime Honeycomb Block, Beehive, Bee Nest Flower Forest, Sunflower Plains Ice Slime Ice, Packed Ice, Snow Block Snowy Plains, Ice Spikes, Frozen Peaks Iron Slime Stone, Deepslate, Block of Iron Dripstone Caves, Windswept Gravelly Hills Luminous Slime Moss Block, Calcite, Glowstone Lush Caves Lunar Slime Calcite, Block of Amethyst, Blue Ice Plains, Meadow, Snowy Plains Magma Slime Magma Block, Basalt, Blackstone Basalt Deltas Magmatic Slime Magma Block, Basalt, Netherrack Nether Wastes, Basalt Deltas, Badlands Moss Slime Moss Block, Mossy Cobblestone, Grass Block Forest, Lush Caves Mud Slime Mud, Packed Mud, Clay Swamp, Mangrove Swamp Mycelium Slime Mycelium, Moss Block, Podzol Mushroom Fields, Lush Caves Obsidian Slime Obsidian, Crying Obsidian, Deepslate Dripstone Caves, Eroded Badlands Prismatic Slime Block of Amethyst, Calcite, Stone Stony Peaks, Dripstone Caves Sand Slime Sand, Red Sand, Sandstone Desert Sculk Slime Sculk, Sculk Catalyst Deep Dark Solar Slime Block of Gold, Sand, Grass Block Plains, Sunflower Plains, Desert Soul Slime Soul Sand, Soul Soil, Bone Block Soul Sand Valley Steam Slime Sand, Gravel, Clay River, Beach Stone Slime Stone, Cobblestone, Deepslate Stony Peaks, Dripstone Caves Storm Slime Grass Block, Stone, Moss Block, Block of Copper, Sand Windswept Hills Supercell Slime Lightning Rod, Grass Block, Stone, Moss Block Windswept Hills Venom Slime Mud, Mycelium, Podzol Mangrove Swamp, Dark Forest Void Slime End Stone, Obsidian, Purpur Block End Barrens Volatile Flame Slime Magma Block, Netherrack, Basalt Savanna, Windswept Hills Water Slime Sand, Gravel, Clay River, Beach Wind Slime Grass Block, Stone, Moss Block Windswept Hills, Windswept Forest"}, {"title": "Incubator", "url": "guides/INCUBATOR.html", "text": "Incubator Accelerate a captured juvenile's growth while preserving its identity, genes, and lineage. Each cycle is started manually by the caretaker. Recipe I G I G B G I R I I = iron ingot; G = glass; B = Breeding Gel; R = redstone. Item ID: slimeevolution:incubator . Start a cycle Capture a juvenile using the normal trust, health, and energy rules. Insert its capsule, compatible food, and Breeding Gel, Genetic Catalyst, or Royal Gel. As its caretaker, press Incubate . Hunger must be below 80, comfort at least 40, and energy at least 20. Wait 200 loaded ticks : ten seconds at 20 ticks per second. Inspect the individual, remove the capsule, or start another cycle if growth remains. Supplement Maximum reduction in remaining growth Breeding Gel 1,200 ticks Genetic Catalyst 2,400 ticks Royal Gel 3,600 ticks A completed cycle consumes one compatible food and one supplement. Each supplement adds 200 ticks of chronological age ; assisted growth and chronological age are separate. The previously determined adult size is preserved. Food reduces hunger by up to 20 and restores up to 10 energy, within the 0–100 limits. Comfort and trust remain unchanged. The meal cooldown becomes 100 ticks. Genome, lineage, metamorphosis, and other cooldowns are preserved; health ratio follows size changes. Incubation does not grant mutations, breeding, trust, or metamorphoses. Missing valid food or supplement pauses work. Changing the specimen cancels without charging. Completing a cycle does not automatically start another. Adults cannot start a cycle, but a completed result remains readable if the juvenile matured. Remove the updated capsule and release it normally. Previous copies no longer represent the valid capture. Care and capture · Materials and supplements"}, {"title": "Slime Levels and Experience", "url": "guides/LEVELS.html", "text": "Slime Levels and Experience Player guide · Companions Bonded slimes have an individual level from 1 to 10 , replacing practice lessons. Follow, Wait, and Return home are available at level 1 . Keep at least 40 trust, mark a home before returning, and respect the five-follower limit. Earn experience Completed action XP Eat one item from the slime's own diet 2 Kill a passive mob 8 Kill a hostile mob 20 Kill one of the four bosses 160 Meals must actually be accepted, respecting hunger, diet, and the five-second feeding interval. Hand-feeding, feeders, and feed bags use the same rule. Wrong foods, repeated attempts during cooldown, analyzer clicks, and defeating another companion award no XP. Boss summons award no XP. Kill XP belongs to the slime that finishes the target, including when Minecraft loot and experience are credited to its caretaker. Projectiles retain that credit. Delayed unattributed damage, such as poison, also counts when the target took actual damage from that slime within the last ten seconds. Direct player kills do not award slime XP. Experience is not automatically shared with the party. Attribute growth Level 1 retains the current species, size, and genetic attributes. Each additional level adds 20% of base health , 18% of base damage , and 1 armor . Both basic attacks and offensive companion skills benefit from damage growth. Armor is capped at 30. At level 10, a slime has 2.8× health , 2.62× damage , and +9 armor compared with level 1. Species rarity and their original attributes still matter. Leveling preserves the current health percentage rather than fully healing the slime. Level Total XP Health Damage Extra armor 1 0 1× 1× 0 2 30 1.2× 1.18× 1 3 90 1.4× 1.36× 2 4 180 1.6× 1.54× 3 5 300 1.8× 1.72× 4 6 450 2× 1.9× 5 7 630 2.2× 2.08× 6 8 840 2.4× 2.26× 7 9 1080 2.6× 2.44× 8 10 1350 2.8× 2.62× 9 The analyzer panel shows level, XP progress, and attributes. Jobs that previously required 20, 40, or 60 training points now require levels 2, 3, or 4. Saves and migration XP and level stay with the individual through saves, capture, release, and metamorphoses. Offspring start at level 1 without inherited XP. Wild slimes start at level 1 and gain XP after bonding. Old training is converted once: each complete twenty points grants one level above the first. For example, 60 points become level 4 and 100 points become level 6. Home, posture, commands, and symbiosis consent are retained. The practice button has been removed. Creative Slime Wand Find the Creative Slime Wand in Slime Evolution's creative tab. Right-click a mod slime to set 100 trust and level 10 . The wand is reusable, has no recipe or loot source, and only works in Creative mode, even if obtained by command in another mode. Wild slimes bond to you; already bonded individuals keep their existing caretaker. Genes, identity, orders, inventory, hunger, comfort, and energy remain intact. Promotion preserves the current health percentage and does not wake a defeated companion. Bosses and vanilla mobs are unaffected. /give @s slimeevolution:creative_slime_wand"}, {"title": "Materials and Recipes", "url": "guides/MATERIALS.html", "text": "Materials and Recipes Use gelatins, essences, and fragments to craft equipment, prepare breeding, and assist growth. Recipes appear in the in-game recipe book. Items use original dimensional SolarPunk models. Shapeless recipes Up to four ingredients fit in the player crafting grid; five or more require a crafting table. Repeated ingredients occupy separate slots. Ingredients Result Slimeball + sugar 1 Basic Gelatin Basic Gelatin + 2 wheat + 2 glow berries 2 Breeding Gel Basic Gelatin + amethyst shard + redstone + blaze powder 2 Genetic Catalysts Amethyst shard + iron nugget 2 Crystal Fragments Basic Gelatin + Elemental Essence + 2 Crystal Fragments 1 Slime Core Basic Gelatin + Elemental Essence + redstone 4 Genetic Catalysts Slime Core + Crystal Fragment + gold ingot + Elemental Essence 2 Mutation Stabilizers Slime Core + Crystal Fragment + Ancestral Essence 4 Mutation Stabilizers Slime Core + glass 1 Slime Capsule Slime Core + 3 iron ingots + glass + 2 redstone 1 Genetic Station Original gel, capsule, analyzer, station, and incubator recipes remain available, so basic research and breeding do not require bosses. Essence recipes return a glass bottle for each essence consumed. Basic Gelatin is an ingredient, not universal slime food. Crystal Fragments are refined items, not Crystal projectiles or automatic substitutes for amethyst. Harvest essences Use a glass bottle on a cared-for living adult. The elemental family supplies Elemental Essence: Fire, Ice, Water, Electric, Wind, and Venom. Ancestral supplies Ancestral Essence. Datapack species using the elemental family follow the same rule. The caretaker needs interaction permission, reach, and line of sight. The adult needs trust ≥60, hunger ≤40, comfort and energy ≥60, and health ≥75%, without combat, breeding readiness, recent capture reaction, mounts, passengers, or leash. An accepted harvest yields one essence , costs 20 energy and +10 hunger , and starts 6,000 loaded ticks of recovery. It does not damage the slime, change genes, or add trust. A rejected harvest charges nothing. Multiple bottles send output to inventory or drop it nearby if full; Creative follows vanilla container behavior. Recovery persists through saves and capsules and pauses while captured or unloaded. The analyzer shows recovery in a tooltip. Only the successful harvester receives that Slimepedia discovery. Stabilize the next birth Apply a Mutation Stabilizer to an eligible parent before Breeding Gel . Normal caretaker, permission, reach, sight, and breeding requirements apply. It consumes one item outside Creative; duplicate applications are rejected without charge. If either parent is protected, the pair's next accepted birth has zero chance of new numeric mutations . Inherited alleles are still selected normally. The child receives known birth history without new changes and does not inherit protection. If both parents are treated, both protections are consumed. Protection survives incompatible pairs, blocked space, canceled births, readiness expiration, saves, capsules, and metamorphoses. Only accepted offspring insertion consumes it. It does not automatically repeat. Incubator supplements Each cycle also needs one compatible food and 200 loaded ticks of processing. Supplement Maximum growth progress Breeding Gel 1,200 ticks Genetic Catalyst 2,400 ticks Royal Gel 3,600 ticks All add only 200 chronological age ticks and preserve genes, birth evidence, parents, species, and adult size. Catalyst does not change mutation chance. See incubation rules . Recipe discoveries Slimeballs unlock Basic Gelatin; gelatin unlocks batch gel and the initial catalyst. Amethyst shards unlock Crystal Fragments. Elemental Essence unlocks the core and essence catalyst. Cores unlock elemental stabilizers and alternate capsule/station recipes. Ancestral Essence unlocks the higher-yield stabilizer. Recipe unlocks and personal Slimepedia research are independent. Old research journals do not gain retroactive harvesting discoveries. Boss materials Royal Gel, Igneous Fragment, Prismatic Shard, and Primordial Essence come from boss victories . A Primordial Seal requires Royal Gel, Igneous Fragment, Prismatic Shard, Nether Star, and Ancient Tablet. It can summon the Primordial boss or transform Void into Ancestral; each accepted use consumes one seal. See ascension ."}, {"title": "Research and Progression", "url": "guides/PROGRESSION.html", "text": "Research and Progression Slimepedia Craft a Slimepedia from one book and one slimeball . Version 0.15.0 also gives each player a book on their first login to a world, once per player. Use it on a live nearby slime to record a species; use it in the air to browse your journal. The book opens in both hands before showing the interface and also works from the offhand. Escape or the close button ends reading. Reduced motion skips the opening transition. Search, filters, four tabs, and a 3D species preview organize discoveries. Tab Knowledge How to unlock it Field Species, temperament, observed habitats Observe with the book Diet Compatible foods Successfully feed manually Genes Ability and genetic research Analyze an individual or capsule Paths Completed crosses and metamorphoses Witness a birth as caretaker or complete a transformation The journal belongs to the player and is shared by all their books. Observation, feeding, and analysis are independent discoveries. Unobserved catalog entries remain hidden; trading books does not transfer research. Analyzer and Genetic Station Use the Genetic Analyzer on a slime to inspect needs, age, ancestry, alleles, and evolution routes. Hover over genes, time information, and the footer for details. The Genetic Station analyzes an occupied capsule. Insert capsule, paper, and redstone, press Analyze, then View genes. A cycle takes 100 loaded ticks and charges on completion. Bond and teams Crouch and use the analyzer on your slime to open training . Teach Wait, Follow, and Return home, mark a safe home, and enable cooperation. Water + Moss help crops; Electric + Iron assist machines. Incubation and inheritance The Incubator accelerates captured juvenile growth. Each manual cycle needs compatible food and a supplement and takes 200 loaded ticks. Genes and lineage remain intact. Breed compatible, well-cared-for adults . Offspring inherit parental alleles and may mutate. Genetic research distinguishes recorded birth mutations from ordinary inheritance and unavailable history. Advanced routes Gather materials , discover crosses and metamorphoses , and challenge bosses for materials used in equipment, incubation, and rare lineages such as Prismatic and Celestial. Online guide and advancements The Online guide button opens the full guide in a browser. Review the address in Minecraft's confirmation dialog; canceling or returning preserves your book view. Version 0.15.0 includes 16 Minecraft advancements for obtaining the book and equipment, research, breeding, metamorphosis, species collections, and boss victories. Open Advancements with L by default."}, {"title": "Circuits, Sonar, and Displays", "url": "guides/SIGNAL_JOBS.html", "text": "Circuits, Sonar, and Displays Electric, Crystal, Energized Crystal, and Glass have dedicated jobs. Crouch and use the analyzer on your slime, then open Job . Species Job Level Cost Electric Living circuit 2 2 energy, +1 hunger per accepted pulse Crystal Mineral sonar 2 4 energy, +2 hunger when an echo is found Energized Crystal Crystal relay 3 1 energy on activation and each second of active signal Glass Living display 1 No energy cost Active jobs need a calm adult, trust 40, energy 30, hunger ≤60, and comfort 40. They start paused. Circuits require building permission and an online caretaker in the same dimension. Electric: adjustable pulses Select Output , use the analyzer on a floor with empty space above, and keep the slime within six blocks and clear line of sight. Set the interval and duration, then enable the job. Intervals are 1, 2, 4, or 8 seconds ; durations are 2, 4, 8, or 10 ticks . Defaults are two seconds and four ticks. Adjustments pause work. Output strength is 15 , supporting redstone, droppers, pistons, and nearby mechanisms. Occupied output space is not replaced and does not charge for rejected pulses. Clearing the link pauses the job. Crystal: mineral sonar Enable the job and press Search . The panel closes to reveal a pulse and a direction with weak, medium, or strong intensity. Scans reach 12 blocks , including through stone, seeking clusters of at least four mineral blocks in one directional sector. Ores and amethyst blocks are recognized; an isolated vein may not produce a useful echo. Scans preserve terrain, respect protected regions, and use loaded chunks only. Recovery is ten seconds , even without an echo; unsuccessful scans preserve energy and hunger. The last echo indicator is temporary, while recovery persists through saves and capsules. Energized Crystal: relay a signal Link a Source block such as a lever, pressure plate, or redstone wire, then a Destination floor with free output space. Keep the slime within six blocks of output and enable the job. Input and output must be loaded, in the same dimension, and 4–32 blocks apart . The relay preserves analog strength 0–15 . No input signal means no energy charge. Output turns off when paused, captured, removed, or when its caretaker becomes unavailable. Temporary output points do not retain power without a valid source after reloading. Circuits respect permissions, arena protection, and mobGriefing . Glass: display an item Place one item in its display compartment. It rotates inside the transparent body. Enlarge increases visual scale; Normal size restores it. The core is hidden while an item is displayed. Display storage needs 40 trust and no energy. Count, durability, name, and enchantments stay intact. Capsules and embedded inventories are rejected. Capture preserves the item and scale; death drops belongings. Existing cargo remains withdrawable. Other jobs · Care and capture"}, {"title": "Slime Species Gallery", "url": "guides/SLIMES.html", "text": "Slime Species Gallery Discover 47 species : 21 natural species and 26 forms acquired through breeding or metamorphosis . Images are real Minecraft captures, cropped and resized. Genes can change color and size. Diets follow the default species data and can be changed by datapacks. Care and capture · Breeding · Evolution · Bosses Natural Species Amethyst Slime Resonance highlights threats; amethyst blocks prolong the effect. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Amethyst Shard, Glow Berries Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Block of Amethyst, Calcite, Smooth Basalt Preferred biomes: Lush Caves, Deep Dark Habitat details slimeevolution:amethyst Common Slime Adaptable, with an unusually elastic jump. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Slimeball, Apple, Wheat Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Grass Block, Moss Block, Slime Block Preferred biomes: Plains, Sunflower Plains Habitat details slimeevolution:common Corrupted Slime Aggressive; deteriorates targets and increases mutation chance in offspring. Temperament: Hostile Diet: Rotten Flesh, Spider Eye Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Sculk, Deepslate, Mossy Cobblestone Preferred biomes: Deep Dark Habitat details slimeevolution:corrupted Electric Slime Defends its territory; discharges spread between wet targets. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Redstone, Glowstone Dust Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Stone, Block of Copper, Sand Preferred biomes: Stony Shore, Savanna Habitat details slimeevolution:electric End Slime Retreats with a short, safe blink when wounded and threatened. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Chorus Fruit, Ender Pearl Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: End Stone, End Stone Bricks, Purpur Block Preferred biomes: End Highlands, End Midlands Habitat details slimeevolution:end Fire Slime Immune to fire; ignites enemies but is hurt by water. Temperament: Hostile Diet: Coal, Blaze Powder Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Magma Block, Netherrack, Basalt Preferred biomes: Nether Wastes, Basalt Deltas, Badlands Habitat details slimeevolution:fire Fungal Slime Spores weaken threats; nearby mushrooms aid recovery. Temperament: Docile Diet: Brown Mushroom, Red Mushroom Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Mycelium, Podzol, Brown Mushroom Block Preferred biomes: Mushroom Fields Habitat details slimeevolution:fungal Ice Slime Chills enemies, resists freezing and is vulnerable to fire. Temperament: Hostile Diet: Snowball, Ice Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Ice, Packed Ice, Snow Block Preferred biomes: Snowy Plains, Ice Spikes, Frozen Peaks Habitat details slimeevolution:ice Iron Slime A heavy body that resists melee blows and knockback. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Iron Nugget, Raw Iron Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Stone, Deepslate, Block of Iron Preferred biomes: Dripstone Caves, Windswept Gravelly Hills Habitat details slimeevolution:iron Luminous Slime An emissive body; helps its caregiver see in dark caves. Temperament: Docile Diet: Glow Berries, Glow Ink Sac Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Moss Block, Calcite, Glowstone Preferred biomes: Lush Caves Habitat details slimeevolution:luminous Magma Slime Recovers in lava and ignites enemies while heated. Temperament: Hostile Diet: Magma Cream, Blaze Powder Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Magma Block, Basalt, Blackstone Preferred biomes: Basalt Deltas Habitat details slimeevolution:magma Moss Slime Regenerates while wet or resting on moss. Temperament: Docile Diet: Moss Block, Glow Berries Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Moss Block, Mossy Cobblestone, Grass Block Preferred biomes: Forest, Lush Caves Habitat details slimeevolution:moss Mud Slime Defends itself by slowing attackers. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Mud, Clay Ball Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Mud, Packed Mud, Clay Preferred biomes: Swamp, Mangrove Swamp Habitat details slimeevolution:mud Obsidian Slime A slow, heavy body protected against explosions. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Obsidian, Crying Obsidian Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Obsidian, Crying Obsidian, Deepslate Preferred biomes: Dripstone Caves, Eroded Badlands Habitat details slimeevolution:obsidian Sand Slime Blends into sand while still and blinds enemies with dust. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Sand, Cactus Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Sand, Red Sand, Sandstone Preferred biomes: Desert Habitat details slimeevolution:sand Soul Slime Moves freely on soul sand; siphons vitality over soul terrain. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Soul Sand, Soul Soil Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Soul Sand, Soul Soil, Bone Block Preferred biomes: Soul Sand Valley Habitat details slimeevolution:souls Stone Slime Heavy armor and knockback resistance, at the cost of speed. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Cobblestone, Flint Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Stone, Cobblestone, Deepslate Preferred biomes: Stony Peaks, Dripstone Caves Habitat details slimeevolution:stone Venom Slime Defends its territory with a short-lived toxic cloud. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Spider Eye, Brown Mushroom Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Mud, Mycelium, Podzol Preferred biomes: Mangrove Swamp, Dark Forest Habitat details slimeevolution:venom Void Slime Pulls a visible nearby threat with a brief spatial impulse. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Popped Chorus Fruit, Ender Pearl Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: End Stone, Obsidian, Purpur Block Preferred biomes: End Barrens Habitat details slimeevolution:void Water Slime Swims efficiently, breathes underwater and pushes enemies with water jets. Temperament: Docile Diet: Kelp, Seagrass Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Sand, Gravel, Clay Preferred biomes: River, Beach Habitat details slimeevolution:water Wind Slime Jumps higher, cushions falls and pushes enemies with gusts. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Feather, Sugar Acquisition: Natural encounter Comfort floor: Grass Block, Stone, Moss Block Preferred biomes: Windswept Hills, Windswept Forest Habitat details slimeevolution:wind Hybrids and Metamorphoses Abyssal Slime A luminous lure guides its dark body and deep-water fins. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Glow Ink Sac, Kelp Acquisition: Metamorphosis from Glacial Aquatic Comfort floor: Prismarine, Dark Prismarine, Blue Ice Preferred biomes: Deep Cold Ocean, Deep Frozen Ocean Habitat details slimeevolution:abyssal Amber Slime Golden resin surrounds a stick, cobblestone and a decorative pickaxe; its touch is sticky. Temperament: Docile Diet: Honeycomb, Wheat Acquisition: Metamorphosis from Moss Comfort floor: Moss Block, Honeycomb Block Preferred biomes: Flower Forest, Sunflower Plains Habitat details slimeevolution:amber Ancestral Slime An advanced metamorphosis that briefly protects a wounded keeper. Temperament: Docile Diet: Golden Carrot, Glistering Melon Slice Acquisition: Metamorphosis from Void Comfort floor: Purpur Block, End Stone Bricks, Block of Gold Preferred biomes: End Highlands Habitat details slimeevolution:ancestral Aurora Slime A gradient of colors and an animated aurora protect nearby allies. Temperament: Docile Diet: Amethyst Shard, Glowstone Dust Acquisition: Metamorphosis from Prismatic Comfort floor: Blue Ice, Packed Ice, Block of Amethyst Preferred biomes: Frozen Peaks, Ice Spikes Habitat details slimeevolution:aurora Bog Slime A docile moss-and-mud hybrid that slows attackers. Temperament: Docile Diet: Clay Ball, Glow Berries Acquisition: Moss + Mud; Moss + Water Comfort floor: Mud, Moss Block, Clay Preferred biomes: Swamp, Mangrove Swamp Habitat details slimeevolution:bog Caustic Slime Its bubbles leave temporary acid pools that weaken enemies. Temperament: Hostile Diet: Spider Eye, Magma Cream Acquisition: Venom + Magma Comfort floor: Mud, Mycelium, Podzol, Magma Block, Basalt, Blackstone Preferred biomes: Swamp Habitat details slimeevolution:caustic Celestial Slime A rare Ancestral metamorphosis using Primordial essence and high stability. Temperament: Docile Diet: Golden Carrot, Glistering Melon Slice Acquisition: Metamorphosis from Ancestral Comfort floor: Purpur Block, End Stone Bricks, Block of Gold Preferred biomes: End Highlands Habitat details slimeevolution:celestial Coral Slime A cluster of branching corals helps allies recover in water. Temperament: Docile Diet: Seagrass, Kelp Acquisition: Water + Floral Comfort floor: Prismarine, Brain Coral Block, Tube Coral Block, Bubble Coral Block Preferred biomes: Warm Ocean Habitat details slimeevolution:coral Crystal Slime Fires crystal shards while retaining mineral protection. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Amethyst Shard, Quartz Acquisition: Metamorphosis from Stone Comfort floor: Block of Amethyst, Calcite, Stone Preferred biomes: Stony Peaks, Dripstone Caves Habitat details slimeevolution:crystal Eclipse Slime A dark silhouette surrounded by a golden corona alternates solar and lunar attacks. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Blaze Powder, Amethyst Shard Acquisition: Solar + Lunar Comfort floor: End Stone, Purpur Block, Obsidian Preferred biomes: End Highlands Habitat details slimeevolution:eclipse Energized Crystal Slime Crystal and Electric share one cooldown for shards and discharge. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Amethyst Shard, Redstone Acquisition: Crystal + Electric Comfort floor: Block of Amethyst, Calcite, Stone Preferred biomes: Stony Peaks, Dripstone Caves Habitat details slimeevolution:energized_crystal Ferrofluid Slime Moving metallic spikes attract metal items dropped by its keeper. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Iron Nugget, Raw Iron Acquisition: Iron + Water Comfort floor: Block of Iron, Block of Copper, Block of Raw Iron Preferred biomes: Stony Shore Habitat details slimeevolution:ferrofluid Floral Slime A flowering moss form that regenerates more frequently. Temperament: Docile Diet: Glow Berries, Dandelion Acquisition: Metamorphosis from Moss Comfort floor: Moss Block, Grass Block, Flowering Azalea Preferred biomes: Forest, Lush Caves Habitat details slimeevolution:floral Glacial Aquatic Slime Water and Ice combine a chilling jet with aquatic movement. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Kelp, Snowball Acquisition: Water + Ice Comfort floor: Ice, Packed Ice, Snow Block Preferred biomes: Frozen River, Frozen Ocean Habitat details slimeevolution:glacial_aquatic Glass Slime Transparent gel with vitrified edges that refract light and projectiles. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Sand, Quartz Acquisition: Sand + Fire Comfort floor: Sand, Glass, Tinted Glass Preferred biomes: Desert Habitat details slimeevolution:glass Hive Slime Dripping honeycombs shelter bees and small temporary pollinators. Temperament: Docile Diet: Honeycomb, Dandelion Acquisition: Metamorphosis from Amber Comfort floor: Honeycomb Block, Beehive, Bee Nest Preferred biomes: Flower Forest, Sunflower Plains Habitat details slimeevolution:hive Lunar Slime Silvery gel with craters and a full moon; its light helps allies at night. Temperament: Docile Diet: Amethyst Shard, Glow Berries Acquisition: Metamorphosis from Luminous Comfort floor: Calcite, Block of Amethyst, Blue Ice Preferred biomes: Plains, Meadow, Snowy Plains Habitat details slimeevolution:lunar Magmatic Slime Heat inherited from fire, with a mineral-reinforced body. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Magma Cream, Blaze Powder Acquisition: Stone + Fire; Metamorphosis from Fire Comfort floor: Magma Block, Basalt, Netherrack Preferred biomes: Nether Wastes, Basalt Deltas, Badlands Habitat details slimeevolution:magmatic Mycelium Slime Filaments and mushrooms spread regenerative spores among allies. Temperament: Docile Diet: Brown Mushroom, Moss Block Acquisition: Fungal + Moss Comfort floor: Mycelium, Moss Block, Podzol Preferred biomes: Mushroom Fields, Lush Caves Habitat details slimeevolution:mycelium Prismatic Slime A rare Crystal metamorphosis with a Colossus trophy and high luminosity. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Amethyst Shard, Quartz Acquisition: Metamorphosis from Crystal Comfort floor: Block of Amethyst, Calcite, Stone Preferred biomes: Stony Peaks, Dripstone Caves Habitat details slimeevolution:prismatic Sculk Slime Warden-like horns detect movement and answer with echo pulses. Temperament: Hostile Diet: Echo Shard, Glow Ink Sac Acquisition: Metamorphosis from Corrupted Comfort floor: Sculk, Sculk Catalyst Preferred biomes: Deep Dark Habitat details slimeevolution:sculk Solar Slime A white-gold core sustains fiery rays and recovery in sunlight. Temperament: Neutral Diet: Blaze Powder, Golden Carrot Acquisition: Metamorphosis from Fire Comfort floor: Block of Gold, Sand, Grass Block Preferred biomes: Plains, Sunflower Plains, Desert Habitat details slimeevolution:solar Steam Slime A hybrid of Fire and Water that clouds an opponent’s sight. Temperament: Docile Diet: Kelp, Blaze Powder Acquisition: Fire + Water Comfort floor: Sand, Gravel, Clay Preferred biomes: River, Beach Habitat details slimeevolution:steam Storm Slime Combines air currents with electrical discharges. Temperament: Hostile Diet: Redstone, Feather Acquisition: Electric + Wind Comfort floor: Grass Block, Stone, Moss Block, Block of Copper, Sand Preferred biomes: Windswept Hills Habitat details slimeevolution:storm Supercell Slime A mature storm cloud with wind rings and chained discharges. Temperament: Hostile Diet: Redstone, Feather Acquisition: Metamorphosis from Storm Comfort floor: Lightning Rod, Grass Block, Stone, Moss Block Preferred biomes: Windswept Hills Habitat details slimeevolution:supercell Volatile Flame Slime Wind and Fire combine a fiery gust, fire immunity and a water weakness. Temperament: Hostile Diet: Blaze Powder, Feather Acquisition: Wind + Fire Comfort floor: Magma Block, Netherrack, Basalt Preferred biomes: Savanna, Windswept Hills Habitat details slimeevolution:volatile_flame"}, {"title": "Slime Materials and Identity", "url": "guides/SLIME_IDENTITIES.html", "text": "Slime Materials and Identity Each species keeps its body shape, core, and expressions. Materials, accessories, and movement communicate its element, even while idle. Gel color still follows genetics. Slime Appearance and movement Celestial Translucent gel, three internal constellations, two tilted orbiting rings, and two pairs of luminous wings with star tips Energized Crystal Twelve differently sized crystals, connecting arcs, and pulsing energy veins Soul Blue spirit flames, three small eyed souls inside the body, and soft side mist Bog Branching roots, varied cattails, floating vegetation, and slow bubbles Mycelium Branching white and lilac filaments, mushrooms at different growth stages, and subtle spores Mud Wet reflections, slow drips, clay volumes, landing splashes, and slower gel animation Obsidian Dark volcanic glass plates, irregular fractures, and purple edge highlights Supercell Three spiraling cloud layers, lightning between body and clouds, and a narrow ground-level tornado Images are real gameplay captures, cropped, resized, and captioned. Each GIF uses four frames of the same individual separated by ten ticks. reducedMotion in config/slimeevolution-client.toml stops decorative animations. Particles remain bounded by client and server settings ."}, {"title": "Individual Slime Jobs", "url": "guides/SPECIALIZATIONS.html", "text": "Individual Slime Jobs The companion panel offers 19 individual jobs . Crouch and use the Genetic Analyzer on your slime, then open Job . See also production, transport, and auras and circuits, sonar, and displays . Requirements Active workers must be calm adults with trust ≥40, energy ≥30, hunger ≤60, comfort ≥40, and no recent damage, combat, breeding, leash, mount, or passengers. Jobs start disabled. The nearby caretaker needs clear line of sight and appropriate permissions. Hover over information icons for costs. Fire: furnace assistant Keep Fire within four blocks and clear line of sight of a furnace, blast furnace, or smoker, under Free or Wait. The caretaker must be online in the same dimension with permission to alter the location. Every second, an available slime adds up to 20 cooking ticks to processing that has already accepted fuel, ingredients, and output space. Each pulse costs 2 energy and +1 hunger , with a 20-tick worker cooldown. Multiple furnaces cannot reuse the same helper simultaneously, and multiple slimes do not multiply that furnace's pulse in the same second. Normal fuel, recipes, output, and XP remain in effect. Invalid or blocked work does not charge. Work respects mobGriefing and NeoForge permissions. Fungal: composter Place eight identical compostable items in the first slot. Vanilla composting inputs such as seeds, leaves, plants, and plant foods are accepted. After 200 loaded work ticks , eight inputs become one bone meal , costing 6 energy and +3 hunger . Slots hold up to 16 items. Invalid input or full output resets the cycle without charging. Pausing or losing care conditions preserves progress, as do saving and capture. Processing can continue while following. Output can be withdrawn with Shift; inputs cannot be placed in the output slot. Abyssal: underwater guide Enable the job while both the slime's and caretaker's eyes are submerged, within six blocks and clear line of sight. It also works while following. When useful, an action restores up to 60 air and grants or refreshes 15 seconds of Night Vision . It costs 2 energy and +1 hunger , with 40 ticks of recovery. Full air and sufficiently recent Night Vision do not charge; longer existing effects are preserved. Granted effects expire normally after leaving water, but further assistance requires both participants to remain submerged. Amber: storage keeper Amber offers three compartments of up to 16 items , respecting each item's normal stack limit. Deposits require 40 trust. Stored objects appear inside its resin body; empty Amber retains its decorative inclusions. Storage requires no processing cycle or energy. Capsules, bags, shulker boxes, and items with embedded inventories are rejected. Shift transfers preserve excess items in the player's inventory. Persistence and withdrawal Items, job preferences, cooldowns, and composting progress persist through saves and capsules. Capture preserves belongings; death drops them once. Offspring begin with empty storage and jobs disabled. Metamorphosis preserves belongings. If the new species lacks that job, withdrawal remains available until its inventory is empty. companions.specializations can pause jobs and deposits without preventing withdrawal or disabling stored work preferences. Jobs do not load chunks; cooldowns advance only while loaded."}, {"title": "Structures and Natural Arenas", "url": "guides/SPECIAL_STRUCTURES.html", "text": "Structures and Natural Arenas Six structures generate in new chunks when structure generation is enabled. Each has its own architecture, materials, lighting, and SolarPunk details. Structure ID after slimeevolution: Allowed biomes Contents royal_court Plains, Sunflower Plains, Swamp 53×53×53 court with four towers, raised galleries, recessed windows, green glazing, processional arches, throne, gardens, and moat. Gelatinous King altar. elemental_sanctuary Plains, Desert, Savanna 53×42×53 temple with a copper-and-glass dome, colonnades, oculus, and four elemental shrines. Magmatic Heart altar. crystal_cavern Stony Peaks, Dripstone Caves, Plains, Forest 49×39×49 geode with giant crystals, mineral bands, stalactites, and a stair-accessible expedition gallery. Crystalline Colossus altar. ancestral_chamber End Highlands, End Midlands 53×49×53 chamber with a high vault, buttresses, side galleries, rose window, and a large three-axis orrery. Primordial Slime altar. gelatinous_lake Swamp, Mangrove Swamp, Plains 49×29×49 lake with organic banks, a boardwalk loop, visible stilts, fishing pier, a covered cabin, a smaller pavilion, and slime islets. researcher_ruins Plains, Forest, Taiga 49×39×49 campus with a two-story library, mezzanine, glazed conservatory, laboratory, observatory, and overgrown ruins. Summon at an altar The four arenas have central engraved pedestals and 17×17 floor space with six clear blocks above . Arena Ritual item Boss Royal Court Gelatinous Crown Gelatinous King Elemental Sanctuary Magma Brazier Magmatic Heart Crystal Cavern Crystal Sigil Crystalline Colossus Ancestral Chamber Primordial Seal Primordial Slime Structures start without bosses. An accepted Survival summon consumes one item. The altar remains reserved until that boss dies, including across unloading and server restarts. Rejected uses do not consume ritual items. After victory, the altar can be reused. Ordinary floors cannot start rituals. In 0.21.0, side clicks also work. Standing on the pedestal or bringing followers no longer automatically blocks the ritual: the boss uses a free nearby position inside the arena. If every position is occupied, the item is preserved and feedback explains the missing space. Rituals remain unavailable on Peaceful difficulty. Arena protection All four boss arenas remain protected before, during, and after fights, including in Creative. Protection covers the structure, foundations, and an outer margin. It blocks breaking, placement, fluid changes, explosion damage to blocks, pistons, and indirect terrain changes from fire, dispensers, falling blocks, fluids, or mobs. Altars, chests, and reward collection remain accessible. Attacks and explosions can still affect entities. Protection persists independently of structure-generation settings. Lakes and researcher ruins are unprotected exploration sites. Exploration and frequency Each structure contains one finite loot chest; opening, emptying, or reloading it does not refill it. The Ancestral Chamber supplies an Ancient Tablet for the Primordial Seal. Loot does not automatically reveal Slimepedia entries. Crystal caverns are underground without an excavated entrance tunnel. Surface sites reject unsuitable oceans, steep terrain, and low islands. There is no retroactive generation: explore new terrain for updated structures and altars. The five Overworld sites share one random_spread placement set with spacing 16 and separation 6 chunks. Each candidate selects only one site, with enough space between neighboring candidates for the largest template plus a buffer. The Ancestral Chamber keeps its separate End set with spacing 24 and separation 8. Biome, height, slope, and rarity filter candidates, so spacing does not guarantee a structure at every interval. Server settings control overall and individual generation plus rarity. With commands enabled, use /locate structure slimeevolution:royal_court in the Overworld or /locate structure slimeevolution:ancestral_chamber in the End. Substitute other IDs as needed. Datapack has_<id> tags can extend allowed biomes. Bosses · Configuration 0.23.0 architecture gallery All six builds are original. Visual research examined facade depth, repeated bays, material hierarchy, circulation, and integrated vegetation in Repurposed Structures: Jungle Fortress , Oak Mansion , End Ancient City , and Flower Forest Pyramid . No external templates were copied. Version 0.23.0 adds framed elevations, timbered gables, cornices, a deeper portal, covered porticoes, a porch, seating, lighting, and planted borders. The rounded geode preserves surrounding terrain, and a glazed drum joins the observatory wall to its dome. Existing structures remain in place; corrected templates appear in new chunks. Interiors include reading, dining, research, and expedition areas. Stairs and mezzanine edges have guardrails, and circulation between wings and floors remains clear. The images below are in-game captures in a flat review meadow. Natural placement follows the biome and slope rules above. Foundations are eight blocks deep, and each build retains one finite reward chest with an accessible interior route. Arenas retain their clear ritual floors. Royal Court The occupied wings contain reading and dining rooms on both floors, with stairs and guardrails. Elemental Sanctuary Crystal Cavern Ancestral Chamber Gelatinous Lake Researcher Ruins Building workflow and comparison The public Build It guides consulted for this revision were Ironcrest Medieval Castle , Ravenwick Tall Gable House , Stonebeam Cottage , and the Outdoor collection . The revision applies recessed entrances, a stone/wood material hierarchy, layered roofs, and paths with seating, plants, and lighting. The mod's structures remain original. The architecture revision uses the Minecraft Builder skill and its building guide : distinct volumes and roofs, recessed facades, consistent materials, circulation between floors, and review in isometric previews and in the game. This is an authoring tool, not a mod dependency. Royal Court in 0.22.1: Royal Court in 0.23.0:"}, {"title": "Production, Transport, and Auras", "url": "guides/WORK_JOBS.html", "text": "Production, Transport, and Auras Crouch and use the analyzer on your slime, then open Job . Work starts paused. Workers need calm adulthood, trust 40, energy 30, hunger at most 60, and comfort 40. Requirements below refer to individual slime levels . Species Job Level Cost per useful action Iron Smith 1 Repair material; 6 energy, +3 hunger Common Courier 2 Linked containers; 2 energy, +1 hunger per pickup or delivery Water Irrigator 1 Stored water; 2 energy, +1 hunger Luminous Light guide 1 Glowstone dust; 1 energy per pulse Soul Memory keeper 2 Recorded last death; 1 energy every two seconds End Passage keeper 4 One pearl; 12 energy, +4 hunger per trip Void Spatial collector 3 Linked container or Amber; 2 energy, +1 hunger Caustic Recycler 2 Equipment and slimeball; 6 energy, +3 hunger Lunar Lunar tides 2 A useful phase effect; 3 energy, +1 hunger Hive Beekeeper 1 Flower and optional bottle; 6 energy, +3 hunger Aurora Peacekeeper 2 Nearby companions; 3 energy, +1 hunger Iron: repair equipment Place a tool or armor piece in the first slot and a compatible repair material in the second. After ten seconds , one material restores 25% of maximum durability , preserving name and enchantments. The equipment stays in its slot for withdrawal or another cycle. Wrong materials and fully repaired equipment do not charge. Supported materials follow the equipment's normal repair rules, including iron, gold, diamond, netherite, cobblestone, planks, leather, turtle scutes, and phantom membrane. Common: deliver between stations Select Source in the panel, then crouch and use the analyzer on a nearby chest or barrel. Repeat for Destination , enable the job, and choose Free. Containers must share a dimension and be within 32 blocks of each other. The slime navigates normally, picks up up to 16 items per operation, and delivers within three blocks. Full output preserves its cargo. Withdraw cargo through the panel. Follow, Wait, and Return home pause the route; the clear button removes links without deleting cargo. Water: irrigation and bottles A water bucket in the first slot fills the reservoir with 1,000 units and returns an empty bucket. Once per second it can hydrate visible farmland within four blocks, spending 25 units . Bottles in slot two and space in slot three allow one water bottle per 100 units . Bottling takes priority over irrigation. Stored water persists through saves and capsules. Luminous: light the way Glowstone dust supplies 20 pulses per item , one per second, lighting the slime's path and its caretaker's path within six blocks. A pulse costs one energy. Temporary lights do not replace existing blocks and expire within three loaded seconds without renewal. Capturing or losing the slime does not create permanent lighting. Soul: find the last death Enable the job near the caretaker. It shows the dimension and coordinates of the player's last death, points with particles in the same dimension, and highlights up to three nearby stacks identified as that player's lost belongings. Track checks the same point with a two-second cooldown. It locates surviving items; it does not recreate missing ones. End: travel between anchors Link source and destination floors through the analyzer, in the same dimension and within 32 blocks . Supply ender pearls, enable the job, stand within four blocks of an anchor, and press Travel . The caretaker and slime travel together. Each accepted trip consumes one pearl, 12 energy, and +4 hunger, with ten seconds of recovery. Both need safe, clear landing space. Blocked, hazardous, or unloaded destinations do not consume a pearl. Void: collect loose items Link a nearby chest, barrel, or Amber belonging to the same caretaker. Once per second, transfer up to 16 items from a visible loose stack within six blocks to the visible destination. Excess remains on the ground. Capsules, embedded inventories, stacks with pickup delay, and other players' identified belongings are excluded. No capacity means no charge. Caustic: recycle metal Insert iron, gold, or chainmail equipment, a slimeball, and leave output space. After ten seconds, consume both inputs and return up to 25% of the metal as nuggets , proportional to remaining durability and capped at 16 nuggets. Enchantments are not transferred. Insufficient yield or output room consumes nothing. Lunar: phase benefits An enabled Lunar supports its caretaker within six blocks and clear line of sight according to its individual phase. Phase Benefit Full Regeneration I when injured Waning gibbous Resistance I Last quarter Haste I Waning crescent Removes Poison and Hunger New Invisibility Waxing crescent Jump Boost I First quarter Speed I Waxing gibbous Night Vision Effects last 15 seconds, with five seconds between actions. Useful refreshes cost three energy and +1 hunger. Stronger existing effects are preserved. See individual phases . Hive: honey and pollination Maintain a visible planted flower within four blocks. Under Free, the slime can seek nearby flowers. A flower in the first slot becomes honeycomb after ten seconds; a bottle in the second produces bottled honey instead. Output uses slot three. A cycle can also advance a nearby crop one stage when permitted. Full output or missing flowers stops processing without charging. Aurora: calm the enclosure Every five seconds, help up to three slimes of the same caretaker within six blocks and clear line of sight. Each receives four comfort and seven seconds of calm, reducing spontaneous aggression and retaliation between companions without disabling self-defense. Useful actions cost three energy and +1 hunger. Persistence and permissions Materials, cargo, water, cooldowns, and links persist through saves and capsules. Metamorphosis pauses the previous job; withdraw belongings and configure the new species. Death drops stored items. Work follows server settings, caretaker permissions, protection events, and mobGriefing where applicable. Only loaded entities and regions are used."}, {"title": "Genetics and Inheritance", "url": "reference/GENETICS.html", "text": "Genetics and Inheritance Each immutable genome contains 15 genes , each with two finite alleles in [0, 1] . Additive expression uses the average, dominant expression the maximum, and recessive expression the minimum. These are fictional gameplay rules; expression does not replace stored alleles. Founders and offspring Natural and spawn-egg founders receive 30 random alleles in [0.25, 0.75) . Directly created entities without spawn finalization retain baseline 0.5/0.5 until assigned a genome. Loading or releasing a capsule preserves existing genes. For each gene, offspring inherit one equally likely allele from each parent. Each inherited allele can mutate independently. Effective probability is: min(0.25, mutationChance × (1.5 - average parental stability) × (1 + 0.5 × unstable parents)) Default mutationChance is 0.02: stability gives 1%–3% per allele without unstable parents. One parent with unstable_touch adds a 1.5 factor; two give a factor of 2. Setting chance to zero disables mutations even for Corrupted parents. There are no spontaneous lifetime mutations or genetic infection from attacks. Mutation adds a random delta between -mutationStep and +mutationStep , clamped to [0, 1] . Default step is 0.1; configurable chance and step cap at 0.25. Parents are unchanged. Gene effects e is expressed value, between zero and one. Species baselines apply at size 2; health and damage use current size divided by two. Gene Expression Effect Size Additive Adult size: min(max, min + floor(e × (max - min + 1))) Elasticity Additive Jump factor 0.75 + 0.5e ; Common offensive knockback 0.35 × (0.5 + e) Vitality Additive Base health × size factor × 0.75 + 0.5e Speed Additive Base speed × 0.8 + 0.4e Metabolism Additive Hunger + 0.1 × (0.5 + e) each loaded second Resistance Dominant Armor base + (e - 0.5) × 4 , clamped 0–20; mineral reduction min(0.75, setting × (0.5 + e)) Fertility Additive Breeding recovery × 1.25 - 0.5e Stability Additive Adjusts mutation probability using parental average Regeneration Recessive Moss healing (0.5 + e) × setting , capped at six health Elemental potency Additive Fire, mud, and chill duration × 0.5 + e and setting, capped at 200 ticks Aggression Dominant Retaliation 100 + 200e ticks; docile flee threshold 0.4 - 0.2e health fraction Sociability Additive Social search radius 4 + 8e ; stopping distance 4 - 2e blocks Transparency Additive Base gel alpha round(255 - 102e) combined with species material Luminosity Recessive Luminous body visual light round(8 + 7e) ; other species do not gain this emission Pigmentation Dominant Species RGB channels × 0.85 + 0.3e , capped at 255 All 15 genes have expression implemented. Transparency is not invisibility. Genetic luminosity is visual emission, not block lighting or a spawn-rule change. At baseline, gel alpha is 204 and Luminous visual emission is 12. Species still determines temperament and ability selection. Lineage, growth, and inspection Lineage stores both parent UUIDs and generation. Founders start at zero; children use the higher parental generation plus one, capped at one million. Self-pairing, parent–child, siblings, and half-siblings are rejected; there is no unlimited ancestral tree. Juveniles begin at size 1 and grow toward their genome-determined adult size, subject to food, comfort, energy, and space. See breeding . Individual NBT version 7 preserves genes, lineage, growth, breeding counters, transformation history and exposure, ecological home, and birth mutation evidence. Old saves retain identities and alleles; unavailable mutation history remains unavailable rather than being inferred. Capsules preserve this state and validate it against the world's capture ledger. The analyzer is read-only and shows identification, ancestry, alleles, needs, counters, birth evidence, and evolution requirements. Evolution and stabilization Hybrids inherit alleles using the normal service and receive the recipe's species. Metamorphoses preserve every allele and the lineage: environmental conditions allow a species change without rewriting the genome. Recessive thresholds require both alleles to qualify. A Mutation Stabilizer applied to an eligible parent before gel prevents new mutations in the next accepted birth . Allele selection and inherited unusual values remain unchanged. Protection persists through failed or canceled births and expires only on accepted offspring insertion. See materials and verified genetic research . Epistasis, environmentally conditioned gene expression, and rare mutation categories are planned rather than current features."}, {"title": "Species and Datapacks", "url": "reference/SPECIES_DATA.html", "text": "Species and Datapacks Species definitions Each data/<namespace>/slime_species/<name>.json defines a species. Its id must match <namespace>:<name> . The mod includes 47 definitions. Field Format id , family Namespaced IDs color Integer RGB, 0–16,777,215 min_size , max_size Integers 1–4, minimum ≤ maximum stats Health 1–200, speed 0.01–0.6, damage 0–30, armor 0–20, elasticity 0.5–1.5 temperament docile , neutral , or hostile ecology solitary , social , or territorial ; default solitary diet Existing item IDs biomes Explicit existing biome IDs natural_spawn Boolean; default true ability Registered mod ability ID ability_cooldown_ticks 20–12,000 ticks ability_energy_cost 0–100 Base species attributes correspond to size 2 before genetic expression. The 26 included derived species use natural_spawn: false . For additional spawn biomes, also extend slimeevolution:spawns_evolution_slimes with replace: false . New species can reuse the entity and existing abilities; new abilities need Java implementation and registration. New IDs are not automatically allowed by basic capsules. Breeding Define pairs under data/<namespace>/slime_breeding/<name>.json : { \"first\": \"slimeevolution:common\", \"second\": \"slimeevolution:common\", \"offspring\": \"slimeevolution:common\" } Parent order does not matter. Duplicate or reversed duplicate pairs are rejected. Missing recipes block a combination. Caretaker, needs, relatedness, and space checks still apply. Metamorphoses Files under data/<namespace>/slime_metamorphosis/ define source, result, catalyst, environment, gene, age, exposure, and costs. Use the 14 included recipes as complete examples. See evolution . Habitats and reloading Preferred floors use data/<namespace>/tags/block/habitat/<species>.json . Add the appropriate tag for habitat evaluation. Run /reload and inspect the log after editing a datapack. Species, breeding, and metamorphoses are validated as one snapshot; invalid data keeps the previous snapshot. Changed routes can invalidate incompatible exposure. /summon slimeevolution:evolution_slime ~ ~ ~ {Species:\"yournamespace:your_species\"} Test appearance, attributes, persistence, and breeding in a test world. Optional environmental conditions These fields belong inside conditions ; old recipes remain valid without them. Field Values / default cycle any , day , night ; default any weather any , clear , rain , thunder ; default any sky_visible Boolean; default false min_y , max_y Inclusive integers −2048 to 2048; defaults −2048 / 2048 moon_phase −1 for any, 0 for full moon, up to 7; default −1 submerged Requires eyes underwater when true; default false Day, night, moon, and sky checks require a dimension with skylight. The analyzer displays these conditions in its biome-line tooltip. Metamorphosis milestones Optional milestone values are storm_charges , biome_journey , and celestial_observations . An empty value preserves old recipes; unknown values are rejected. Milestones supplement rather than replace care, genes, exposure, and catalyst checks. See ascension requirements ."}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.10.0", "url": "updates/0.10.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.10.0 Version history · Player guide Celestial appearances and lunar phases Eclipse receives a spherical aura and orbiting Sun and Moon. Ferrofluid gains small head spikes. Lunar receives eight persistent individual phases with a floating moon, independent of the world calendar. Steam emits rising, expanding, dissipating smoke across its surface. The update does not create additional species. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.11.0", "url": "updates/0.11.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.11.0 Version history · Player guide Animated elemental materials Corrupted gains a dark coating with moving iridescent patches and colored fissures. Lunar gains 20 craters with bright rims and shaded centers. Solar gains slowly rotating rays and corona, individual pulses, and rippling plasma. The changes are decorative, preserve Lunar’s eight phases, and respect reduced motion. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.12.0", "url": "updates/0.12.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.12.0 Version history · Player guide Structures, ascension, and more jobs Six structures gain expanded architecture, including the new Royal Court. Four protected boss arenas use reusable ritual altars and retain encounter reservations through unloading and restarts. Eleven jobs add repairs, transport, irrigation, lighting, death tracking, anchor travel, collection, recycling, lunar benefits, beekeeping, and calming. Eclipse, Supercell, Aurora, Ancestral, and Celestial gain dedicated ascension milestones. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.13.0", "url": "updates/0.13.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.13.0 Version history · Player guide Four signal and display jobs The total reaches 19 individual jobs . Electric produces adjustable redstone pulses; Crystal performs directional mineral sonar; Energized Crystal relays analog signals between linked input and output; Glass displays and enlarges a real item inside its body. Links, recovery, settings, and stored items persist through saves and capsules. Circuits respect arena protection and shut down when their source becomes unavailable. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.14.0", "url": "updates/0.14.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.14.0 Version history · Player guide Eight renewed visual identities Celestial gains internal constellations, orbital rings, and luminous wings. Energized Crystal gains varied crystals, pulsing veins, and electrical arcs. Soul gains small internal spirits and blue flames. Bog gains roots, cattails, vegetation, and bubbles. Mycelium gains branching filaments and mushrooms. Mud gains wet surfaces, drips, and landing splashes. Obsidian gains volcanic glass plates and fractures. Supercell gains layered clouds, lightning, and a focused tornado. These decorative changes preserve body shape, expressions, and gameplay and respect reduced motion. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.14.1", "url": "updates/0.14.1.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.14.1 Version history · Player guide Online guide and panoramic banner The Slimepedia gains an Online guide button, using Minecraft’s address confirmation dialog and preserving book search and selection when returning. The guide supports topic navigation, search, a gallery, mobile layout, and offline distribution. A real-game panoramic banner features eight species, six items, and three machines. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.14.2", "url": "updates/0.14.2.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.14.2 Version history · Player guide A dedicated public guide The illustrated player guide moves to its own public repository, Slime-Evolution-Mod-Docs. Guides, references, images, and version history are published separately from the mod’s source code. The Slimepedia’s Online guide button opens the new address. Navigation, search, and the gallery remain available; gameplay and slime appearances are unchanged. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.15.0", "url": "updates/0.15.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.15.0 Version history · Player guide A Slimepedia for every new player Each player receives one Slimepedia on their first login to a world, with persistent delivery tracking across death, reconnection, and dimension changes. A full inventory drops the book at the player’s feet; an existing carried book avoids duplication. Existing worlds receive delivery on the first login after updating. The original crafting recipe remains available. A new Minecraft advancement tab adds 16 milestones , with English and Portuguese text: obtain the book and equipment; discover the first species and collections of 10 and 47; feed, analyze, breed, and transform slimes; defeat each boss and all four. Research milestones can recognize existing journal progress; boss milestones require new player-credited victories. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.16.0", "url": "updates/0.16.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.16.0 Version history · Player guide Companion combat postures The bond panel adds Passive , Defensive (default), and Aggressive , independently of movement commands. Defensive responds to attacks on the caretaker or slime and assists against the caretaker's recent attack target. Aggressive also seeks visible hostiles within 16 blocks. Passive does not automatically attack or retaliate. Caretakers, companions, tame animals, and protected players remain excluded. Postures persist through saves, capsules, and metamorphoses. Labels and tooltips are available in English and Portuguese. Companion contact now damages the selected mob, extending vanilla slime contact behavior beyond players and iron golems. Five followers Each caretaker can have five Follow reservations across all dimensions. Unloaded followers retain their slots. Capturing a follower or changing its movement command frees a slot. Capsules and older saves cannot exceed the cap: excess followers switch to Wait while keeping their other data. Requirements, range, and controls ."}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.17.0", "url": "updates/0.17.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.17.0 Version history · Player guide Companion skills by acquisition tier All 47 species have dedicated attacks or support skills across five acquisition tiers and five roles: brawler, tank, ranged, support, and skirmisher. Attacks have visible windups, range, energy costs, and recovery. Walls block projectiles; healing and shielding use shared recipient limits. Water prepares electrical combos, Ice builds chill, Caustic reduces armor, Eclipse alternates phases, and Celestial combines an 18-base-damage attack with an eight-health caretaker shield. Rare species provide broader effects at higher costs. Combat postures and the five-follower limit still apply. Browse the complete companion combat catalog . Stronger boss encounters Boss Health Armor Gelatinous King 600 10 Magmatic Heart 750 12 Crystalline Colossus 900 16 Primordial Slime 1,024 14 The initial damage factor rises from 1.5 to 2 while preserving phase scaling and attack warnings. Minions can attack companions, and nearby tanks attract more pressure. Royal guards, healers, and spitters gain health; royal healing restores 14 health per pulse. Other servants have 32 health. Existing bosses with canonical attributes migrate while preserving their health ratio. This initial balance pass aims to reward teams of three to five companions with complementary roles. Update the mod on both client and server; GeckoLib 4.9.3 remains required. A boss finished by a bonded companion now credits its present caretaker for boss loot and the kill advancement."}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.18.0", "url": "updates/0.18.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.18.0 Version history · Player guide Keep your team together Follow receives faster hopping and more frequent path updates outside combat. Ancestral and Celestial can follow in the air with real collision-aware navigation. A follower more than 32 blocks away can catch up by teleporting to safe, dry, supported ground near its caretaker in the same dimension. Unsafe space, combat, exhaustion, and unavailable or unloaded entities do not bypass the checks. The five-follower cap remains. Defeat instead of permanent loss Bonded companions fall into a 10-second defeated state on lethal ordinary damage. Three orbiting stars mark recovery; they stay still and stop attacking and working. They recover with half health and brief protection while retaining their identity, bond, training, orders, and belongings. Recovery persists across saves and pauses while unloaded. Wild slimes and administrative removal retain normal death behavior. Movement, teleport, and recovery rules . Find the right floor The habitat reference lists all 47 species, accepted floor blocks, and comfort biomes. Each gallery card now includes these preferences and a direct link. Inherited tags are expanded into block names. The guide explains floor contact, non-stacking bonuses, gradual adjustment, and crowding penalties. Update the mod on both client and server. GeckoLib 4.9.3 remains required."}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.19.0", "url": "updates/0.19.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.19.0 Version history · Player guide Food for your followers The Royal Feed Bag stores five food stacks and uses the Gelatinous King's Royal Gel. Upgrade it with one Igneous Fragment from the Magmatic Heart for fifteen slots, preserving food and the bag's custom name. Carry it to feed only your own following slimes within sixteen blocks, respecting diets and normal meal cooldowns. Recipes and behavior . Companions keep responding at low energy Low energy no longer blocks learned movement, autonomous Aggressive target selection, or basic attacks. Ranged companions without enough energy for their next special move into melee instead of waiting at firing distance. Special skills still cost their listed energy. A projectile already launched can land even when paying its cost left the caster below twenty energy. Unfunded melee attacks now use the normal attack reach instead of requiring a physical collision after navigation stops. Winged followers can also take longer routes around nearby walls without expanding the checked loaded region. The changes were exercised with Ancestral, Celestial, and Eclipse against zombies and the Magmatic Heart, including transitions to Defensive and Passive. Update the mod on client and server; GeckoLib 4.9.3 remains required."}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.2.0-visual.1", "url": "updates/0.2.0-visual.1.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.2.0-visual.1 Version history · Player guide The first visual rework The first visual pass builds on the functional release candidate. Six primary slimes receive integrated hierarchies and atlases with observed idle, jump, damage, and feeding actions. Six priority artifacts gain dimensional models. Interfaces, blocks, other species, and broader polish remain work in progress at this historical stage. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.2.0-visual.2", "url": "updates/0.2.0-visual.2.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.2.0-visual.2 Version history · Player guide Distinct creature anatomy All 32 species, four bosses, and the royal minion gain their own anatomy and integrated rendering. Entity registrations, genetics, and capture are preserved. The next visual release introduces droplet bodies. Current appearances are shown in the species gallery. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.2.0-visual.3", "url": "updates/0.2.0-visual.3.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.2.0-visual.3 Version history · Player guide Command-summoned boss fix Bosses summoned with commands could ignore Survival players because missing arena positions were assigned before command placement. Missing arena origins are now initialized on the first AI tick at the correct position. Explicit saved arenas, including the world origin, remain intact; NoAI still intentionally disables AI. Damage, ritual costs, IDs, hitboxes, and schemas are unchanged. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.2.0-visual.4", "url": "updates/0.2.0-visual.4.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.2.0-visual.4 Version history · Player guide Droplet bodies and elemental effects The 32 species, four bosses, and royal minion receive droplet-shaped bodies and distinct elemental effects. The visual direction includes head flames, liquid splashes, branching electricity, poison bubbles and vapor, stone over gel, and luminous liquid. Geometry and artwork are original. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.20.0", "url": "updates/0.20.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.20.0 Version history · Player guide Levels 1–10 replace training lessons. Follow and Wait are available at level 1. Food and kills grant XP; each level increases health, armor, and attack damage. The panel shows XP and attributes. Old training migrates once. Values and rules . Ancestral and Celestial flap their wings while flying , using mirrored strokes and a steady spread with reduced motion. Renewed elemental attacks: eight visual families, original four-frame textures, luminous projectiles with tapered trails, expanding impacts, beams, and richer high-rarity sigils. Effects respect distance and visual quality limits. Ally protection: caretakers and their slimes cannot damage their own bonded slimes. Attributed melee, projectiles, explosions, and harmful effects are rejected without losing trust or energy. Healing and buffs still work. Other players, enemies, and unattributed hazards such as lava and block fire keep their normal rules. Fall immunity for all 47 species, wild or bonded, and royal minions. Update both client and server. GeckoLib 4.9.3 remains required."}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.20.1", "url": "updates/0.20.1.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.20.1 Version history · Player guide Adds the Creative Slime Wand , usable only in Creative mode. Right-click a mod slime to grant 100 trust and maximum level (10). Find it in the mod's creative tab. It is reusable and has no recipe or loot source. Wild slimes bond to the player; existing caretakers and other individual data are preserved. How to use . Update both client and server. GeckoLib 4.9.3 remains required."}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.21.0", "url": "updates/0.21.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.21.0 Version history · Player guide Fixes all four pedestals: side clicks work, and summoning finds a free position when the player or followers occupy the center. Permission, space, and Peaceful failures provide feedback without consuming the item. Companions continue basic attacks between special skills. Defensive finishes engaged fights, Aggressive avoids unnecessary target changes, pursuit tolerates brief obstructions, and wounded bonded slimes do not use wild docile panic. Skill costs, ally protection, and Passive stance remain enforced. Rebuilds all six structures with larger layouts, deeper facades, galleries, domes, glazing, interiors, boardwalks, and landscaping. Materials, routes to rewards, and ritual spaces are validated in Minecraft. Gallery and references . The new builds appear in new chunks; existing generated builds are not replaced. Update client and server. GeckoLib 4.9.3 remains required."}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.22.0", "url": "updates/0.22.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.22.0 Version history · Player guide Fixes combat continuity for all four bosses: brief visibility tolerance, eligible companion targets, and recovery after displacement beyond the inner arena boundary. Twelve prolonged-combat cases cover attacks, minions, cover, and arena return. Rebuilds all six structures using the Minecraft Builder skill and preview review: inhabited castle wings and roofs, an enclosed circular temple, a cathedral with full facades, an L-shaped library and observatory, a lake cabin with curved boardwalks, and an ellipsoidal cavern. Routes to all six reward chests were checked in Minecraft. Gallery, comparison, and building skill . New builds require new chunks; existing generated structures are not replaced. Update both client and server. GeckoLib 4.9.3 remains required."}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.22.1", "url": "updates/0.22.1.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.22.1 Version history · Player guide Fixes parts of the same building crossing occupied spaces: the L-shaped library junction, the observatory interior, and the Ancestral Chamber's spires and aisle roofs. Connects roofs, domes, stained glass, stairs, and structural details to their foundations. Roof stairs now rise continuously toward the ridge, with outward-facing inverted eaves. Foliage no longer replaces roofs or walls; lake islets now have submerged bases. Repairs staircase approaches, direction, and support, and moves crystals away from the expedition gallery stairs. The five Overworld sites now share one placement set, selecting only one structure at each candidate and keeping neighboring candidates far enough apart. The Ancestral Chamber keeps its separate End placement. Updated structure gallery . Update both client and server. These fixes appear in new chunks ; structures already generated in your world are not rebuilt automatically. GeckoLib 4.9.3 remains required."}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.23.0", "url": "updates/0.23.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.23.0 Version history · Player guide Adds exterior detail to all six sites: recessed window frames, timbered gables, cornices, roof accents, paths, and planted borders. The Royal Court gains articulated side and rear elevations; the library gains timbered gables, exterior conservatory columns, and observatory cornices. The Ancestral Chamber gains upper gallery windows, a deeper portal, and spire bands. The Sanctuary gains roofed porticoes. The Lake cabin gains attic glazing and a lower porch roof, and compact trees replace crowns clipped at the template edges. Clears tower entrances blocked by window sills and removes an elevated shortcut crossing the Royal Court's upper room. The geode has a rounded shell within the template bounds. Placement preserves surrounding terrain while still excavating the occupied interior. Furnishes and organizes the interiors: Royal reading/dining rooms, library mezzanine and rear reading room, workstations, cabin and pavilion, and ancestral/expedition galleries. Adds guardrails while keeping circulation clear. Updated gallery and comparison . Update both client and server. These changes appear in new chunks ; existing structures are not rebuilt automatically. GeckoLib 4.9.3 remains required."}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.3.0", "url": "updates/0.3.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.3.0 Version history · Player guide Expanded boss patterns Boss encounters gain additional patterns, a more varied royal minion group, and enhanced gel deformation. This historical release documents the progression of combat and presentation; current costs, encounters, and species rules are in the player guide. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.4.0", "url": "updates/0.4.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.4.0 Version history · Player guide GeckoLib and SolarPunk presentation Models adopt GeckoLib animation for movement, feeding, damage, transformation, and boss actions. GeckoLib 4.9.3 becomes a required separate mod on both client and server. Layered gel and elemental materials, original textures, equipment, and interfaces develop the SolarPunk visual direction. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.5.0", "url": "updates/0.5.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.5.0 Version history · Player guide Elemental details and boss encounters Slimes receive expanded elemental accessories while retaining the gel shape and GeckoLib animation system. Bosses gain larger bodies, stronger phase-based attacks, expanded minions, and filled attack areas. Care, breeding, and rare metamorphoses continue to use persistent individual identities. Historical balance values belong to this release; consult the current guides before playing. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.6.0", "url": "updates/0.6.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.6.0 Version history · Player guide Refined elemental anatomy Sixteen species receive visual refinements while preserving gel bodies, faces, and gameplay. Changes include additional crystals, broader Corrupted fissures, an ender-pearl-like End core, varied Floral flowers, icy Glacial Aquatic fins, a faceted Ice shell, and Magmatic volcanic crust. GeckoLib 4.9.3 remains required. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.7.0", "url": "updates/0.7.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.7.0 Version history · Player guide The catalog reaches 47 species Fifteen acquired species expand the catalog from 32 to 47 , with 61 breeding pairs and 14 metamorphoses . Breeding adds Storm, Coral, Glass, Ferrofluid, Mycelium, and Caustic. Metamorphoses add Amber, Abyssal, Sculk, Solar, and Lunar. Advanced forms include Supercell, Hive, Aurora, and Eclipse. Each gains its own gel profile, accessories, atlas, and GeckoLib animations. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.7.1", "url": "updates/0.7.1.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.7.1 Version history · Player guide A book you can hold The Slimepedia becomes a dimensional book with raised cover, stitched spine, brass corners, pages, and bookmark. The player raises and opens it with both hands before reading, including offhand use, and other players see the pose. The item catalog receives dimensional SolarPunk models for tools, capsules, materials, rewards, and spawn eggs. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.7.2", "url": "updates/0.7.2.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.7.2 Version history · Player guide Dimensional machines and nests The Feeder, Genetic Station, and Incubator receive dimensional SolarPunk models with wood, ceramic, brass, glass, and vegetation. Machines face the player when placed; station and incubator monitors animate only during real processing. Surface nests gain roots, moss, flowers, and gel; underground colonies gain stone and luminous fungi. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.7.3", "url": "updates/0.7.3.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.7.3 Version history · Player guide SolarPunk interfaces Five interfaces gain textured paper, copper and brass frames, sage panels, botanical details, custom icons, and recessed slots. The Slimepedia gains a species index, highlighted tabs, research markers, and a 3D preview while retaining private research. Genetic inspection combines a preview, needs, alleles, expression, and evolution requirements. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.8.0", "url": "updates/0.8.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.8.0 Version history · Player guide Training and symbiosis Caretakers can crouch and use the analyzer on their slime to open a companion panel. Lessons teach Wait, Follow, and Return home; sociability and stability affect learning. Commands use normal navigation and prioritize self-defense. Training, home, and preferences persist through saves, capsules, and metamorphoses but are not inherited. Water + Moss assist crops; Electric + Iron assist station and incubator processing, with consent and shared care requirements. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Slime Evolution 0.9.0", "url": "updates/0.9.0.html", "text": "Slime Evolution 0.9.0 Version history · Player guide The first individual jobs Fire assists active furnaces, smokers, and blast furnaces. Fungal converts eight compostables to one bone meal. Abyssal restores air and supports underwater vision. Amber stores items in three compartments and shows them inside its body. Belongings persist through saves, capsules, and metamorphoses and drop once on death. Withdrawal remains possible when server settings disable jobs. Current species gallery · Current gameplay guides"}, {"title": "Version History", "url": "updates/index.html", "text": "Version History These entries summarize the player-facing changes in each release. Historical versions describe their own state; use the player guide for current rules. Version Highlights 0.23.0 Detailed facades, framed gables, porticoes, gardens, and a rounded geode shell. 0.22.1 Clear room junctions, supported roofs and stairs, and shared structure spacing. 0.22.0 Boss combat continuity and architecture rebuilt with Minecraft Builder 0.21.0 Working pedestal interactions, continuous combat, and six rebuilt structures. 0.20.1 Creative-only wand granting 100 trust and level 10. 0.20.0 Levels 1–10, XP from food and kills, animated wings, elemental effects, and ally protection. 0.19.0 Five- and fifteen-slot feed bags; fixes followers freezing at low energy. 0.18.0 Faster Follow, winged flight, safe catch-up, defeated companion recovery, and all habitat floors. 0.17.0 47 companion combat profiles, elemental combos, support limits, and stronger bosses. 0.16.0 Companion combat postures and five followers per caretaker 0.15.0 A Slimepedia for every new player 0.14.2 A dedicated public guide 0.14.1 Online guide and panoramic banner 0.14.0 Eight renewed visual identities 0.13.0 Four signal and display jobs 0.12.0 Structures, ascension, and more jobs 0.11.0 Animated elemental materials 0.10.0 Celestial appearances and lunar phases 0.9.0 The first individual jobs 0.8.0 Training and symbiosis 0.7.3 SolarPunk interfaces 0.7.2 Dimensional machines and nests 0.7.1 A book you can hold 0.7.0 The catalog reaches 47 species 0.6.0 Refined elemental anatomy 0.5.0 Elemental details and boss encounters 0.4.0 GeckoLib and SolarPunk presentation 0.3.0 Expanded boss patterns 0.2.0-visual.4 Droplet bodies and elemental effects 0.2.0-visual.3 Command-summoned boss fix 0.2.0-visual.2 Distinct creature anatomy 0.2.0-visual.1 The first visual rework"}];
